":["3.85%","92.86%","3.70%","0.00%"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Total cost = purchase price + transport. Percentage profit = profit ÷ total cost × 100.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-math-gen-034","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"If x² -19x +90 = 0, what is the sum of the squares of its roots?","options":["181","361","90","183"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The roots are r₁ and r₂. Their squared sum is r₁²+r₂²=(r₁+r₂)²−2r₁r₂.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-math-gen-036","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"An arithmetic progression has first term 10 and common difference 2. What is its 15th term?","options":["38","40","36","180"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Use Tₙ = a + (n−1)d.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-math-gen-037","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Simplify 9^5 × 9^5.","options":["3486784401","717897987691852588770249","1","10000000000"],"answer":0,"explanation":"For equal bases, indices are added when multiplying powers.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-math-gen-038","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A sector has radius 11 cm and central angle 90°. What is its area in terms of π?","options":["121/4π cm²","121π cm²","121/2π cm²","484π cm²"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Sector area = θ/360 × πr².","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-math-gen-039","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Solve simultaneously: 4x + 2y = 56 and 2x + 4y = 58. What is the value of x?","options":["9","10","8","11"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Use elimination or substitution; the simultaneous equations give x as the stated value.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-math-gen-040","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A box contains 10 red and 11 blue counters. Two counters are drawn without replacement. What is the probability that both are red?","options":["3/14","10/21","11/42","20/21"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Multiply the probability of drawing a red first by the probability of drawing a red second without replacement.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-math-gen-041","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Four test scores have mean 57. Three scores are 51, 61 and 54. What is the fourth score?","options":["62","57","65","59"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The total of four scores is 4×mean; subtract the three known scores.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-math-gen-042","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A circular tank has radius 10 cm. What is the ratio of its circumference to its area?","options":["2/10","1/10","10/2","2/11"],"answer":0,"explanation":"C/A = 2πr ÷ πr² = 2/r.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-math-gen-043","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Find the square of 