086","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A sector has radius 15 cm and central angle 75°. What is its area in terms of π?","options":["375/8π cm²","225π cm²","375/4π cm²","1080π cm²"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Sector area = θ/360 × πr².","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-math-gen-087","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Solve simultaneously: 3x + 6y = 123 and 6x + 3y = 120. What is the value of x?","options":["13","14","12","15"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Use elimination or substitution; the simultaneous equations give x as the stated value.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-math-gen-088","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A box contains 14 red and 15 blue counters. Two counters are drawn without replacement. What is the probability that both are red?","options":["13/58","14/29","15/58","28/29"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Multiply the probability of drawing a red first by the probability of drawing a red second without replacement.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-math-gen-089","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Four test scores have mean 61. Three scores are 55, 65 and 58. What is the fourth score?","options":["66","61","69","63"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The total of four scores is 4×mean; subtract the three known scores.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-math-gen-090","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A circular tank has radius 14 cm. Wh