:"","passage":"","q":"A 9 kg trolley increases its speed from 11 m/s to 18 m/s. What impulse acts on it?","options":["63 N s","162 N s","99 N s","261 N s"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Impulse equals change in momentum: m(v−u).","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-019","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A resistor of 10 Ω carries a current of 9 A. What electrical power is dissipated?","options":["810 W","90 W","19 W","1.11111 W"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Power P=I²R or VI.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-020","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A wave has frequency 12 Hz and wavelength 0.55 m. Calculate its speed.","options":["6.6 m/s","21.8182 m/s","12.55 m/s","0.0458333 m/s"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Wave speed v=fλ.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-021","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A 3 kg object moves at 11 m/s in a circle of radius 9 m. What is the magnitude of its centripetal force?","options":["40.3333 N","3.66667 N","297 N","3267 N"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Centripetal force is mv²/r.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-022","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A converging lens has focal length 0.24 m and forms a real image when an object is 0.65 m from it. What is the image distance?","options":["0.380 m","0.175 m","0.410 m","0.156 m"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Use the lens formula 1/f=1/u+1/v with consistent sign conventions for magnitudes in this real-object case.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-023","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"How much heat is needed to raise the temperature of 9 kg of water by 12 °C? Take c=4200 J kg⁻¹ °C⁻¹.","options":["453,600 J","37,800 J","50,400 J","45,360.0 J"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Heat supplied Q=mcΔT.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-024","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Light of wavelength 460 nm falls on a surface. Using h=6.63×10⁻³⁴ J s and c=3.0×10⁸ m/s, what is the energy of one photon?","options":["4.324e-19 J","1.017e-48 J","2.162e-19 J","9.149e-32 J"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Photon energy is E=hc/λ.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-025","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A car travels with initial speed 16 m/s and uniform acceleration 5 m/s² for 5 s. What distance does it cover?","options":["142.5 m","80 m","205 m","62.5 m"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Use s = ut + ½at².","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-026","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A 10 kg object is acted upon by a resultant force of 50 N. What acceleration does it acquire?","options":["5 m/s²","50 m/s²","10 m/s²","6 m/s²"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Newton’s second law gives a=F/m.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-027","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A load of mass 11 kg is lifted vertically through 12 m. Taking g=10 m/s², what increase in gravitational potential energy occurs?","options":["1320 J","132 J","110 J","660 J"],"answer":0,"explanation":"ΔPE=mgh.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-028","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A 10 kg trolley increases its speed from 12 m/s to 20 m/s. What impulse acts on it?","options":["80 N s","200 N s","120 N s","320 N s"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Impulse equals change in momentum: m(v−u).","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-029","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A resistor of 3 Ω carries a current of 10 A. What electrical power is dissipated?","options":["300 W","30 W","13 W","0.3 W"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Power P=I²R or VI.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-030","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A wave has frequency 13 Hz and wavelength 0.2 m. Calculate its speed.","options":["2.6 m/s","65 m/s","13.2 m/s","0.0153846 m/s"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Wave speed v=fλ.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-031","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A 4 kg object moves at 12 m/s in a circle of radius 10 m. What is the magnitude of its centripetal force?","options":["57.6 N","4.8 N","480 N","5760 N"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Centripetal force is mv²/r.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-032","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A converging lens has focal length 0.1 m and forms a real image when an object is 0.7 m from it. What is the image distance?","options":["0.117 m","0.087 m","0.600 m","0.070 m"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Use the lens formula 1/f=1/u+1/v with consistent sign conventions for magnitudes in this real-object case.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-033","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"How much heat is needed to raise the temperature of 10 kg of water by 5 °C? Take c=4200 J kg⁻¹ °C⁻¹.","options":["210,000 J","42,000 J","21,000 J","21,000.0 J"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Heat supplied Q=mcΔT.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-034","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Light of wavelength 480 nm falls on a surface. Using h=6.63×10⁻³⁴ J s and c=3.0×10⁸ m/s, what is the energy of one photon?","options":["4.144e-19 J","1.061e-48 J","2.072e-19 J","9.547e-32 J"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Photon energy is E=hc/λ.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false}],"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"test-physics-3","title":"Physics UTME Standard CBT 3","subject":"Physics","duration":40,"published":true,"shuffleQuestions":true,"shuffleOptions":true,"questions":[{"id":"qb-physics-roman-clean-009","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about a 82 kg body moving on a straight track are correct?\n\nI. If the resultant force is non-zero, its velocity changes.\nII. If the resultant force is zero, the body may still move at constant velocity.\nIII. For a given mass, doubling the resultant force doubles the acceleration.\nIV. Acceleration is measured in newtons.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; acceleration is measured in m/s², while the newton is a unit of force.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":true},{"id":"qb-physics-roman-clean-029","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about a circuit containing a 85 Ω resistor carrying 4 A are correct?\n\nI. The potential difference across the resistor is 340 V.\nII. The electrical power is 1360 W.\nIII. Ohm’s law gives V=IR for an ohmic resistor at constant physical conditions.\nIV. The resistance is found by multiplying voltage by current.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; resistance is R=V/I, not VI.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":true},{"id":"qb-physics-roman-clean-010","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about a wave of frequency 88 Hz and wavelength 1.09 m are correct?\n\nI. Its speed is fλ.\nII. Its period is 1/f.\nIII. If frequency increases while wavelength remains fixed, speed increases.\nIV. Frequency is measured in metres.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; frequency is measured in hertz.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":true},{"id":"qb-physics-roman-clean-030","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about a 87 kg object raised through 4 m are correct, taking g=10 m/s²?\n\nI. Its gravitational potential energy increases by mgh.\nII. The increase is 3480 J.\nIII. Raising it higher increases its gravitational potential energy.\nIV. Gravitational potential energy is measured in watts.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; energy is measured in joules, while the watt is a unit of power.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":true},{"id":"qb-physics-roman-clean-011","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about a 86 kg body moving on a straight track are correct?\n\nI. If the resultant force is non-zero, its velocity changes.\nII. If the resultant force is zero, the body may still move at constant velocity.\nIII. For a given mass, doubling the resultant force doubles the acceleration.\nIV. Acceleration is measured in newtons.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; acceleration is measured in m/s², while the newton is a unit of force.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":true},{"id":"qb-physics-roman-clean-031","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about a circuit containing a 89 Ω resistor carrying 3 A are correct?\n\nI. The potential difference across the resistor is 267 V.\nII. The electrical power is 801 W.\nIII. Ohm’s law gives V=IR for an ohmic resistor at constant physical conditions.\nIV. The resistance is found by multiplying voltage by current.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; resistance is R=V/I, not VI.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":true},{"id":"qb-physics-roman-clean-012","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about a wave of frequency 92 Hz and wavelength 1.13 m are correct?\n\nI. Its speed is fλ.\nII. Its period is 1/f.\nIII. If frequency increases while wavelength remains fixed, speed increases.\nIV. Frequency is measured in metres.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; frequency is measured in hertz.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":true},{"id":"qb-physics-roman-clean-032","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about a 91 kg object raised through 8 m are correct, taking g=10 m/s²?\n\nI. Its gravitational potential energy increases by mgh.\nII. The increase is 7280 J.\nIII. Raising it higher increases its gravitational potential energy.\nIV. Gravitational potential energy is measured in watts.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; energy is measured in joules, while the watt is a unit of power.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":true},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-035","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"How much heat is needed to raise the temperature of 11 kg of water by 6 °C? Take c=4200 J kg⁻¹ °C⁻¹.","options":["277,200 J","46,200 J","25,200 J","27,720.0 J"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Heat supplied Q=mcΔT.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-036","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Light of wavelength 500 nm falls on a surface. Using h=6.63×10⁻³⁴ J s and c=3.0×10⁸ m/s, what is the energy of one photon?","options":["3.978e-19 J","1.105e-48 J","1.989e-19 J","9.945e-32 J"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Photon energy is E=hc/λ.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-038","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A car travels with initial speed 18 m/s and uniform acceleration 2 m/s² for 7 s. What distance does it cover?","options":["175 m","126 m","224 m","49 m"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Use s = ut + ½at².","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-039","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A 12 kg object is acted upon by a resultant force of 84 N. What acceleration does it acquire?","options":["7 m/s²","84 m/s²","12 m/s²","8 m/s²"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Newton’s second law gives a=F/m.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-040","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A load of mass 13 kg is lifted vertically through 5 m. Taking g=10 m/s², what increase in gravitational potential energy occurs?","options":["650 J","65 J","130 J","325 J"],"answer":0,"explanation":"ΔPE=mgh.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026