ge":"","q":"In a large randomly mating population, the frequency of an autosomal recessive allele is 0.11. Assuming Hardy–Weinberg conditions, what is the expected frequency of heterozygotes?","options":["0.20","0.01","0.79","1.00"],"answer":0,"explanation":"With q as the recessive-allele frequency, p=1−q and heterozygotes occur at 2pq.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-bio-gen-046","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"If a producer stores 13,000 kJ of chemical energy and approximately 10% is transferred to the next trophic level, how much energy is available there?","options":["1,300 kJ","130 kJ","6,500 kJ","12,000 kJ"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Using the ecological efficiency approximation, 10% of the energy is transferred to the next trophic level.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-bio-gen-056","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"In a cross between two heterozygous plants with alleles S and s, where S is dominant for smooth and s is recessive for rough, what proportion of offspring is expected to show rough?","options":["25%","50%","75%","100%"],"answer":0,"explanation":"A heterozygous × heterozygous cross gives a 1:2:1 genotype ratio and therefore 25% recessive phenotype.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-bio-gen-076","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A plant transpires at an average rate of 4 cm³ of water per hour for 12 hours. How much water is lost in that period?","options":["48 cm³","16 cm³","0.33 cm³","52 cm³"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Total water loss = rate × time.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-bio-gen-086","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"In a healthy adult, alveolar oxygen partial pressure is 99 mmHg while venous blood oxygen partial pressure is 36 mmHg. Which gas will diffuse from the alveolus into the blood?","options":["Oxygen","Carbon dioxide","Nitrogen","Water vapour"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Oxygen moves down its partial-pressure gradient from alveolar air into venous blood.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-bio-gen-096","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which process most directly contributes to genetic variation by a nucleotide sequence?","options":["gene mutation","binary fission","mitosis","cytokinesis"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Gene mutation contributes to genetic variation in the stated context.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-bio-gen-106","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A population contains 2700 organisms. In one year there are 169 births, 98 deaths, 51 immigrants and 34 emigrants. What is the net increase?","options":["88","71","17","98"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Net population change = births − deaths + immigration − emigration.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1000","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which hormone is most directly associated with the following physiological effect: maintain the uterine lining during pregnancy?","options":["progesterone","insulin","thyroxine","ADH"],"answer":0,"explanation":"progesterone has the stated physiological role.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1001","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which structure is best adapted to translocate organic solutes?","options":["phloem sieve tubes — translocate organic solutes","lysosomes — digest cellular materials","tendons — attach muscles to bones","villi — increase absorptive surface area in the small intestine"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Phloem sieve tubes is specialised for the stated function.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1002","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which option correctly matches ciliated epithelial cells with its principal role?","options":["ciliated epithelial cells — movement of mucus","guard cells — stomatal regulation","liver — detoxification and bile production","phloem — organic solutes"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The selected structure is correctly matched with its principal role.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1003","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"In a large randomly mating population, the frequency of an autosomal recessive allele is 0.12. Assuming Hardy–Weinberg conditions, what is the expected frequency of heterozygotes?","options":["0.21","0.01","0.77","1.00"],"answer":0,"explanation":"With q as the recessive-allele frequency, p=1−q and heterozygotes occur at 2pq.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1004","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"If a producer stores 13,500 kJ of chemical energy and approximately 10% is transferred to the next trophic level, how much energy is available there?","options":["1,350 kJ","135 kJ","6,750 kJ","12,500 kJ"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Using the ecological efficiency approximation, 10% of the energy is transferred to the next trophic level.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1005","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"In a cross between two heterozygous plants with alleles A and a, where A is dominant for long and a is recessive for short, what proportion of offspring is expected to show short?","options":["25%","50%","75%","100%"],"answer":0,"explanation":"A heterozygous × heterozygous cross gives a 1:2:1 genotype ratio and therefore 25% recessive phenotype.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1006","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A plant transpires at an average rate of 5 cm³ of water per hour for 5 hours. How much water is lost in that period?","options":["25 cm³","10 cm³","1.00 cm³","30 cm³"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Total water loss = rate × time.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1007","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"In a healthy adult, alveolar oxygen partial pressure is 101 mmHg while venous blood oxygen partial pressure is 37 mmHg. Which gas will diffuse from the alveolus into the blood?","options":["Oxygen","Carbon dioxide","Nitrogen","Water vapour"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Oxygen moves down its partial-pressure gradient from alveolar air into venous blood.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1008","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which process most directly contributes to genetic variation by the orientation of homologous pairs?","options":["independent assortment","binary fission","mitosis","cytokinesis"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Independent assortment contributes to genetic variation in the stated context.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1009","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A population contains 2800 organisms. In one year there are 176 births, 102 deaths, 54 immigrants and 36 emigrants. What is the net increase?","options":["92","74","18","102"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Net population change = births − deaths + immigration − emigration.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1010","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which hormone is most directly associated with the following physiological effect: stimulate follicle development?","options":["FSH","insulin","thyroxine","ADH"],"answer":0,"explanation":"FSH has the stated physiological role.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1011","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which structure is best adapted to transport oxygen efficiently?","options":["red blood cells — transport oxygen efficiently","guard cells — control stomatal opening","ligaments — connect bone to bone","alveoli — provide a large surface area for gas exchange"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Red blood cells is specialised for the stated function.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1012","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which option correctly matches muscle fibres with its principal role?","options":["muscle fibres — contraction","sperm cells — fertilisation of the ovum","pancreas — digestive enzymes and hormones","red blood cells — oxygen"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The selected structure is correctly matched with its principal role.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1013","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"In a large randomly mating population, the frequency of an autosomal recessive allele is 0.13. Assuming Hardy–Weinberg conditions, what is the expected frequency of heterozygotes?","options":["0.23","0.02","0.76","1.00"],"answer":0,"explanation":"With q as the recessive-allele frequency, p=1−q and heterozygotes occur at 2pq.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1015","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"If a producer stores 14,000 kJ of chemical energy and approximately 10% is transferred to the next trophic level, how much energy is available there?","options":["1,400 kJ","140 kJ","7,000 kJ","13,000 kJ"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Using the ecological efficiency approximation, 10% of the energy is transferred to the next trophic level.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false}],"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"test-biology-3","title":"Biology UTME Standard CBT 3","subject":"Biology","duration":40,"published":true,"shuffleQuestions":true,"shuffleOptions":true,"questions":[{"id":"qb-biology-roman-clean-009","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about the plasma membrane of a liver cell maintained at approximately 105 °C are correct?\n\nI. The membrane is selectively permeable.\nII. Phospholipids form the basic bilayer.\nIII. Some membrane proteins facilitate movement of substances.\nIV. Every substance crosses the membrane by simple diffusion.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; some substances require facilitated diffusion or active transport.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":true},{"id":"qb-biology-roman-clean-029","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about inheritance in a diploid organism with 83 chromosome pairs are correct?\n\nI. Alleles are alternative forms of a gene.\nII. Meiosis can generate new allele combinations.\nIII. DNA carries hereditary information.\nIV. Every mutation produces a harmful phenotype.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; mutations may be harmful, neutral or beneficial.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":true},{"id":"qb-biology-roman-clean-010","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about a population of 9400 organisms are correct?\n\nI. Births can increase population size.\nII. Deaths can reduce population size.\nIII. Immigration can increase population size.\nIV. Emigration always increases population size.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; emigration removes individuals from the population.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":true},{"id":"qb-biology-roman-clean-030","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about human regulation are correct when blood glucose is approximately 319 mg/dL?\n\nI. Insulin helps lower blood glucose concentration.\nII. ADH promotes water reabsorption in the kidney.\nIII. Negative feedback helps maintain internal stability.\nIV. Hormones act only on cells that have no receptors for them.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; hormones exert effects through appropriate receptors.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":true},{"id":"qb-biology-roman-clean-011","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about the plasma membrane of a guard cell maintained at approximately 109 °C are correct?\n\nI. The membrane is selectively permeable.\nII. Phospholipids form the basic bilayer.\nIII. Some membrane proteins facilitate movement of substances.\nIV. Every substance crosses the membrane by simple diffusion.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; some substances require facilitated diffusion or active transport.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":true},{"id":"qb-biology-roman-clean-031","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about inheritance in a diploid organism with 87 chromosome pairs are correct?\n\nI. Alleles are alternative forms of a gene.\nII. Meiosis can generate new allele combinations.\nIII. DNA carries hereditary information.\nIV. Every mutation produces a harmful phenotype.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; mutations may be harmful, neutral or beneficial.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":true},{"id":"qb-biology-roman-clean-012","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about a population of 9800 organisms are correct?\n\nI. Births can increase population size.\nII. Deaths can reduce population size.\nIII. Immigration can increase population size.\nIV. Emigration always increases population size.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; emigration removes individuals from the population.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":true},{"id":"qb-biology-roman-clean-032","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about human regulation are correct when blood glucose is approximately 331 mg/dL?\n\nI. Insulin helps lower blood glucose concentration.\nII. ADH promotes water reabsorption in the kidney.\nIII. Negative feedback helps maintain internal stability.\nIV. Hormones act only on cells that have no receptors for them.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; hormones exert effects through appropriate receptors.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":true},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1016","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"In a large randomly mating population, the frequency of an autosomal recessive allele is 0.14. Assuming Hardy–Weinberg conditions, what is the expected frequency of heterozygotes?","options":["0.24","0.02","0.74","1.00"],"answer":0,"explanation":"With q as the recessive-allele frequency, p=1−q and heterozygotes occur at 2pq.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1017","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"If a producer stores 14,500 kJ of chemical energy and approximately 10% is transferred to the next trophic level, how much energy is available there?","options":["1,450 kJ","145 kJ","7,250 kJ","13,500 kJ"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Using the ecological efficiency approximation, 10% of the energy is transferred to the next trophic level.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1018","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"In a cross between two heterozygous plants with alleles D and d, where D is dominant for dark and d is recessive for light, what proportion of offspring is expected to show light?","options":["25%","50%","75%","100%"],"answer":0,"explanation":"A heterozygous × heterozygous cross gives a 1:2:1 genotype ratio and therefore 25% recessive phenotype.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1019","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A plant transpires at an average rate of 2 cm³ of water per hour for 7 hours. How much water is lost in that period?","options":["14 cm³","9 cm³","0.29 cm³","16 cm³"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Total water loss = rate × time.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1020","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"In a healthy adult, alveolar oxygen partial pressure is 105 mmHg while venous blood oxygen partial pressure is 39 mmHg. Which gas will diffuse from the alveolus into the blood?","options":["Oxygen","Carbon dioxide","Nitrogen","Water vapour"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Oxygen moves down its partial-pressure gradient from alveolar air into venous blood.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1022","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which process most directly contributes to genetic variation by the union of different gametes?","options":["random fertilisation","binary fission","mitosis","cytokinesis"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Random fertilisation contributes to genetic variation in the stated context.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1023","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A population contains 3000 organisms. In one year there are 190 births, 110 deaths, 60 immigrants and 40 emigrants. What is the net increase?","options":["100","80","20","110"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Net population change = births − deaths + immigration − emigration.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1025","type":"mcq","passageId":"","pa