false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1031","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"If a producer stores 15,000 kJ of chemical energy and approximately 10% is transferred to the next trophic level, how much energy is available there?","options":["1,500 kJ","150 kJ","7,500 kJ","14,000 kJ"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Using the ecological efficiency approximation, 10% of the energy is transferred to the next trophic level.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1032","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"In a cross between two heterozygous plants with alleles E and e, where E is dominant for early and e is recessive for late, what proportion of offspring is expected to show late?","options":["25%","50%","75%","100%"],"answer":0,"explanation":"A heterozygous × heterozygous cross gives a 1:2:1 genotype ratio and therefore 25% recessive phenotype.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1033","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A plant transpires at an average rate of 3 cm³ of water per hour for 8 hours. How much water is lost in that period?","options":["24 cm³","11 cm³","0.38 cm³","27 cm³"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Total water loss = rate × time.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1034","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"In a healthy adult, alveolar oxygen partial pressure is 107 mmHg while venous blood oxygen partial pressure is 40 mmHg. Which gas will diffuse from the alveolus into the blood?","options":["Oxygen","Carbon dioxide","Nitrogen","Water vapour"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Oxygen moves down its partial-pressure gradient from alveolar air into venous blood.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1036","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which process most directly contributes to genetic variation by a change in genetic material?","options":["mutation","binary fission","mitosis","cytokinesis"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Mutation contributes to genetic variation in the stated context.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1037","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A population contains 3100 organisms. In one year there are 197 births, 114 deaths, 63 immigrants and 42 emigrants. What is the net increase?","options":["104","83","21","114"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Net population change = births − deaths + immigration − emigration.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1039","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which hormone is most directly associated with the following physiological effect: raise blood calcium concentration?","options":["parathyroid hormone","insulin","thyroxine","ADH"],"answer":0,"explanation":"parathyroid hormone has the stated physiological role.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1040","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which structure is best adapted to carry out photosynthesis?","options":["chloroplasts — carry out photosynthesis","cartilage — reduce friction at joints","villi — increase absorptive surface area in the small intestine","stomata — regulate gaseous exchange and water loss"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Chloroplasts is specialised for the stated function.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1043","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which option correctly matches guard cells with its principal role?","options":["guard cells — stomatal regulation","kidneys — excretion and osmoregulation","stomata — gaseous exchange","neurones — nerve impulses"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The selected structure is correctly matched with its principal role.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1044","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"In a large randomly mating population, the frequency of an autosomal recessive allele is 0.16. Assuming Hardy–Weinberg conditions, what is the expected frequency of heterozygotes?","options":["0.27","0.03","0.71","1.00"],"answer":0,"explanation":"With q as the recessive-allele frequency, p=1−q and heterozygotes occur at 2pq.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1045","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"If a producer stores 15,500 kJ of chemical energy and approximately 10% is transferred to the next trophic level, how much energy is available there?","options":["1,550 kJ","155 kJ","7,750 kJ","14,500 kJ"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Using the ecological efficiency approximation, 10% of the energy is transferred to the next trophic level.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1046","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"In a cross between two heterozygous plants with alleles F and f, where F is dominant for full and f is recessive for small, what proportion of offspring is expected to show small?","options":["25%","50%","75%","100%"],"answer":0,"explanation":"A heterozygous × heterozygous cross gives a 1:2:1 genotype ratio and therefore 25% recessive phenotype.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1047","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A plant transpires at an average rate of 4 cm³ of water per hour for 9 hours. How much water is lost in that period?","options":["36 cm³","13 cm³","0.44 cm³","40 cm³"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Total water loss = rate × time.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1048","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"In a healthy adult, alveolar oxygen partial pressure is 109 mmHg while venous blood oxygen partial pressure is 35 mmHg. Which gas will diffuse from the alveolus into the blood?","options":["Oxygen","Carbon dioxide","Nitrogen","Water vapour"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Oxygen moves down its partial-pressure gradient from alveolar air into venous blood.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1050","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which process most directly contributes to genetic variation by new allele combinations?","options":["recombination","binary fission","mitosis","cytokinesis"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Recombination contributes to genetic variation in the stated context.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1051","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A population contains 3200 organisms. In one year there are 204 births, 118 deaths, 66 immigrants and 44 emigrants. What is the net increase?","options":["108","86","22","118"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Net population change = births − deaths + immigration − emigration.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1053","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which hormone is most directly associated with the following physiological effect: lower blood calcium concentration?","options":["calcitonin","insulin","thyroxine","ADH"],"answer":0,"explanation":"calcitonin has the stated physiological role.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1054","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which structure is best adapted to digest cellular materials?","options":["lysosomes — digest cellular materials","tendons — attach muscles to bones","alveoli — provide a large surface area for gas exchange","xylem vessels — conduct water and mineral salts"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Lysosomes is specialised for the stated function.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1057","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which option correctly matches sperm cells with its principal role?","options":["sperm cells — fertilisation of the ovum","liver — detoxification and bile production","xylem — water and mineral salts","ciliated epithelial cells — movement of mucus"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The selected structure is correctly matched with its principal role.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1058","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"In a large randomly mating population, the frequency of an autosomal recessive allele is 0.17. Assuming Hardy–Weinberg conditions, what is the expected frequency of heterozygotes?","options":["0.28","0.03","0.69","1.00"],"answer":0,"explanation":"With q as the recessive-allele frequency, p=1−q and heterozygotes occur at 2pq.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1059","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"If a producer stores 16,000 kJ of chemical energy and approximately 10% is transferred to the next trophic level, how much energy is available there?","options":["1,600 kJ","160 kJ","8,000 kJ","15,000 kJ"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Using the ecological efficiency approximation, 10% of the energy is transferred to the next trophic level.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false}],"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"test-biology-4","title":"Biology UTME Standard CBT 4","subject":"Biology","duration":40,"published":true,"shuffleQuestions":true,"shuffleOptions":true,"questions":[{"id":"qb-biology-roman-clean-013","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about the plasma membrane of a liver cell maintained at approximately 145 °C are correct?\n\nI. The membrane is selectively permeable.\nII. Phospholipids form the basic bilayer.\nIII. Some membrane proteins facilitate movement of substances.\nIV. Every substance crosses the membrane by simple diffusion.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; some substances require facilitated diffusion or active transport.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":true},{"id":"qb-biology-roman-clean-033","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about inheritance in a diploid organism with 123 chromosome pairs are correct?\n\nI. Alleles are alternative forms of a gene.\nII. Meiosis can generate new allele combinations.\nIII. DNA carries hereditary information.\nIV. Every mutation produces a harmful phenotype.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; mutations may be harmful, neutral or beneficial.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":true},{"id":"qb-biology-roman-clean-014","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about a population of 13400 organisms are correct?\n\nI. Births can increase population size.\nII. Deaths can reduce population size.\nIII. Immigration can increase population size.\nIV. Emigration always increases population size.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; emigration removes individuals from the population.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":true},{"id":"qb-biology-roman-clean-034","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about human regulation are correct when blood glucose is approximately 439 mg/dL?\n\nI. Insulin helps lower blood glucose concentration.\nII. ADH promotes water reabsorption in the kidney.\nIII. Negative feedback helps maintain internal stability.\nIV. Hormones act only on cells that have no receptors for them.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; hormones exert effects through appropriate receptors.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":true},{"id":"qb-biology-roman-clean-015","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about the plasma membrane of a guard cell maintained at approximately 149 °C are correct?\n\nI. The membrane is selectively permeable.\nII. Phospholipids form the basic bilayer.\nIII. Some membrane proteins facilitate movement of substances.\nIV. Every substance crosses the membrane by simple diffusion.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; some substances require facilitated diffusion or active transport.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":true},{"id":"qb-biology-roman-clean-035","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about inheritance in a diploid organism with 127 chromosome pairs are correct?\n\nI. Alleles are alternative forms of a gene.\nII. Meiosis can generate new allele combinations.\nIII. DNA carries hereditary information.\nIV. Every mutation produces a harmful phenotype.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; mutations may be harmful, neutral or beneficial.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":true},{"id":"qb-biology-roman-clean-016","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about a population of 13800 organisms are correct?\n\nI. Births can increase population size.\nII. Deaths can reduce population size.\nIII. Immigration can increase population size.\nIV. Emigration always increases population size.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; emigration removes individuals from the population.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":true},{"id":"qb-biology-roman-clean-036","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about human regulation are correct when blood glucose is approximately 451 mg/dL?\n\nI. Insulin helps lower blood glucose concentration.\nII. ADH promotes water reabsorption in the kidney.\nIII. Negative feedback helps maintain internal stability.\nIV. Hormones act only on cells that have no receptors for them.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; hormones exert effects through appropriate receptors.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":true},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1060","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"In a large randomly mating population, the frequency of an autosomal recessive allele is 0.18. Assuming Hardy–Weinberg conditions, what is the expected frequency of heterozygotes?","options":["0.30","0.03","0.67","1.00"],"answer":0,"explanation":"With q as the recessive-allele frequency, p=1−q and heterozygotes occur at 2pq.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1061","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"If a producer stores 16,500 kJ of chemical energy and approximately 10% is transferred to the next trophic level, how much energy is available there?","options":["1,650 kJ","165 kJ","8,250 kJ","15,500 kJ"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Using the ecological efficiency approximation, 10% of the energy is transferred to the next trophic level.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1062","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"In a cross between two heterozygous plants with alleles K and k, where K is dominant for large and k is recessive for small, what proportion of offspring is expected to show small?","options":["25%","50%","75%","100%"],"answer":0,"explanation":"A heterozygous × heterozygous cross gives a 1:2:1 genotype ratio and therefore 25% recessive phenotype.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1064","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A plant transpires at an average rate of 6 cm³ of water per hour for 11 hours. How much water is lost in that period?","options":["66 cm³","17 cm³","0.55 cm³","72 cm³"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Total water loss = rate × time.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1065","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"In a healthy adult, alveolar oxygen partial pressure is 113 mmHg while venous blood oxygen partial pressure is 37 mmHg. Which gas will diffuse from the alveolus into the blood?","options":["Oxygen","Carbon dioxide","Nitrogen","Water vapour"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Oxygen moves down its partial-pressure gradient from alveolar air into venous blood.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1067","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which process most directly contributes to genetic variation by maternal and paternal homologues?","options":["independent assortment","binary fission","mitosis","cytokinesis"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Independent assortment contributes to genetic variation in the stated context.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1068","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A population contains 3400 organisms. In one year there are 218 births, 126 deaths, 72 immigrants and 48 emigrants. What is the net increase?","options":["116","92","24","126"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Net population change = births − deaths + immigration − emigration.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1071","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which hormone is most directly associated with the following physiological effect: increase sodium reabsorption in the kidney?","options":["aldosterone","insulin","thyroxine","ADH"],"answer":0,"explanation":"aldosterone has the stated physiological role.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1072","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which structure is best adapted to speed up impulse conduction?","options":["myelin sheath — speed up impulse conduction","cilia — move mucus and trapped particles","nephrons — filter blood and form urine","red blood cells — transport oxygen efficiently"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Myelin sheath is specialised for the stated function.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1073","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which option correctly matches testes with its principal role?","options":["testes — sperm and testosterone","trachea — air passage","red blood cells — oxygen","palisade cells — photosynthesis"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The selected structure is correctly matched with its principal role.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1074","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"In a large randomly mating population, the frequency of an autosomal recessive allele is 0.19. Assuming Hardy–Weinberg conditions, what is the expected frequency of heterozygotes?","options":["0.31","0.04","0.66","1.00"],"answer":0,"explanation":"With q as the recessive-allele frequency, p=1−q and heterozygotes occur at 2pq.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1075","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"If a producer stores 17,000 kJ of chemical energy and approximately 10% is transferred to the next trophic level, how much energy is available there?","options":["1,700 kJ","170 kJ","8,500 kJ","16,000 kJ"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Using the ecological efficiency approximation, 10% of the energy is transferred to the next trophic level.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1076","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"In a cross between two heterozygous plants with alleles L and l, where L is dominant for long and l is recessive for short, what proportion of offspring is expected to show short?","options":["25%","50%","75%","100%"],"answer":0,"explanation":"A heterozygous × heterozygous cross gives a 1:2:1 genotype ratio and therefore 25% recessive phenotype.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1078","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A plant transpires at an average rate of 2 cm³ of water per hour for 12 hours. How much water is lost in that period?","options":["24 cm³","14 cm³","0.17 cm³","26 cm³"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Total water loss = rate × time.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1079","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"In a healthy adult, alveolar oxygen partial pressure is 115 mmHg while venous blood oxygen partial pressure is 38 mmHg. Which gas will diffuse from the alveolus into the blood?","options":["Oxygen","Carbon dioxide","Nitrogen","Water vapour"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Oxygen moves down its partial-pressure gradient from alveolar air into venous blood.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1081","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which process most directly contributes to genetic variation by gamete union?","options":["random fertilisation","binary fission","mitosis","cytokinesis"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Random fertilisation contributes to genetic variation in the stated context.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1082","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A population contains 3500 organisms. In one year there are 225 births, 130 deaths, 75 immigrants and 50 emigrants. What is the net increase?","options":["120","95","25","130"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Net population change = births − deaths + immigration − emigration.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1085","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which hormone is most directly associated with the following physiological effect: support the stress response and metabolism?","options":["cortisol","insulin","thyroxine","ADH"],"answer":0,"explanation":"cortisol has the stated physiological role.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1086","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which structure is best adapted to permit communication between neurones?","options":["synapses — permit communication between neurones","microvilli — increase absorptive surface area","stomata — regulate gaseous exchange and water loss","mitochondria — carry out aerobic respiration"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Synapses is specialised for the stated function.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1087","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which option correctly matches kidneys with its principal role?","options":["kidneys — excretion and osmoregulation","alveoli — gas exchange","white blood cells — immune defence","root hairs — water absorption"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The selected structure is correctly matched with its principal role.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1088","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"In a large randomly mating population, the frequency of an autosomal recessive allele is 0.20. Assuming Hardy–Weinberg conditions, what is the expected frequency of heterozygotes?","options":["0.32","0.04","0.64","1.00"],"answer":0,"explanation":"With q as the recessive-allele frequency, p=1−q and heterozygotes occur at 2pq.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1089","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"If a producer stores 17,500 kJ of chemical energy and approximately 10% is transferred to the next trophic level, how much energy is available there?","options":["1,750 kJ","175 kJ","8,750 kJ","16,500 kJ"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Using the ecological efficiency approximation, 10% of the energy is transferred to the next trophic level.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1090","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"In a cross between two heterozygous plants with alleles M and m, where M is dominant for mature and m is recessive for immature, what proportion of offspring is expected to show immature?","options":["25%","50%","75%","100%"],"answer":0,"explanation":"A heterozygous × heterozygous cross gives a 1:2:1 genotype ratio and therefore 25% recessive phenotype.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1092","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A plant transpires at an average rate of 3 cm³ of water per hour for 5 hours. How much water is lost in that period?","options":["15 cm³","8 cm³","0.60 cm³","18 cm³"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Total water loss = rate × time.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1093","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"In a healthy adult, alveolar oxygen partial pressure is 117 mmHg while venous blood oxygen partial pressure is 39 mmHg. Which gas will diffuse from the alveolus into the blood?","options":["Oxygen","Carbon dioxide","Nitrogen","Water vapour"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Oxygen moves down its partial-pressure gradient from alveolar air into venous blood.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1095","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which process most directly contributes to genetic variation by DNA replication or repair errors?","options":["mutation","binary fission","mitosis","cytokinesis"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Mutation contributes to genetic variation in the stated context.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1096","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A population contains 3600 organisms. In one year there are 232 births, 134 deaths, 78 immigrants and 52 emigrants. What is the net increase?","options":["124","98","26","134"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Net population change = births − deaths + immigration − emigration.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1099","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which hormone is most directly associated with the following physiological effect: promote glycogen formation?","options":["insulin","glucagon","thyroxine","ADH"],"answer":0,"explanation":"insulin has the stated physiological role.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1100","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which structure is best adapted to reduce friction at joints?","options":["cartilage — reduce friction at joints","villi — increase absorptive surface area in the small intestine","xylem vessels — conduct water and mineral salts","ribosomes — synthesise proteins"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Cartilage is specialised for the stated function.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1101","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which option correctly matches liver with its principal role?","options":["liver — detoxification and bile production","stomata — gaseous exchange","platelets — blood clotting","guard cells — stomatal regulation"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The selected structure is correctly matched with its principal role.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1102","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"In a large randomly mating population, the frequency of an autosomal recessive allele is 0.21. Assuming Hardy–Weinberg conditions, what is the expected frequency of heterozygotes?","options":["0.33","0.04","0.62","1.00"],"answer":0,"explanation":"With q as the recessive-allele frequency, p=1−q and heterozygotes occur at 2pq.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1103","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"If a producer stores 18,000 kJ of chemical energy and approximately 10% is transferred to the next trophic level, how much energy is available there?","options":["1,800 kJ","180 kJ","9,000 kJ","17,000 kJ"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Using the ecological efficiency approximation, 10% of the energy is transferred to the next trophic level.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false}],"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"test-biology-5","title":"Biology UTME Standard CBT 5","subject":"Biology","duration":40,"published":true,"shuffleQuestions":true,"shuffleOptions":true,"questions":[{"id":"qb-biology-roman-clean-017","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about the plasma membrane of a liver cell maintained at approximately 185 °C are correct?\n\nI. The membrane is selectively permeable.\nII. Phospholipids form the basic bilayer.\nIII. Some membrane proteins facilitate movement of substances.\nIV. Every substance crosses the membrane by simple diffusion.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; some substances require facilitated diffusion or active transport.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":true},{"id":"qb-biology-roman-clean-037","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about inheritance in a diploid organism with 163 chromosome pairs are correct?\n\nI. Alleles are alternative forms of a gene.\nII. Meiosis can generate new allele combinations.\nIII. DNA carries hereditary information.\nIV. Every mutation produces a harmful phenotype.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; mutations may be harmful, neutral or beneficial.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":true},{"id":"qb-biology-roman-clean-018","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about a population of 17400 organisms are correct?\n\nI. Births can increase population size.\nII. Deaths can reduce population size.\nIII. Immigration can increase population size.\nIV. Emigration always increases population size.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; emigration removes individuals from the population.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":true},{"id":"qb-biology-roman-clean-038","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about human regulation are correct when blood glucose is approximately 559 mg/dL?\n\nI. Insulin helps lower blood glucose concentration.\nII. ADH promotes water reabsorption in the kidney.\nIII. Negative feedback helps maintain internal stability.\nIV. Hormones act only on cells that have no receptors for them.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; hormones exert effects through appropriate receptors.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":true},{"id":"qb-biology-roman-clean-019","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about the plasma membrane of a guard cell maintained at approximately 189 °C are correct?\n\nI. The membrane is selectively permeable.\nII. Phospholipids form the basic bilayer.\nIII. Some membrane proteins facilitate movement of substances.\nIV. Every substance crosses the membrane by simple diffusion.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; some substances require facilitated diffusion or active transport.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":true},{"id":"qb-biology-roman-clean-039","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about inheritance in a diploid organism with 167 chromosome pairs are correct?\n\nI. Alleles are alternative forms of a gene.\nII. Meiosis can generate new allele combinations.\nIII. DNA carries hereditary information.\nIV. Every mutation produces a harmful phenotype.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; mutations may be harmful, neutral or beneficial.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":true},{"id":"qb-biology-roman-clean-020","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about a population of 17800 organisms are correct?\n\nI. Births can increase population size.\nII. Deaths can reduce population size.\nIII. Immigration can increase population size.\nIV. Emigration always increases population size.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; emigration removes individuals from the population.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":true},{"id":"qb-biology-roman-clean-040","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about human regulation are correct when blood glucose is approximately 571 mg/dL?\n\nI. Insulin helps lower blood glucose concentration.\nII. ADH promotes water reabsorption in the kidney.\nIII. Negative feedback helps maintain internal stability.\nIV. Hormones act only on cells that have no receptors for them.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; hormones exert effects through appropriate receptors.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":true},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1104","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"In a large randomly mating population, the frequency of an autosomal recessive allele is 0.22. Assuming Hardy–Weinberg conditions, what is the expected frequency of heterozygotes?","options":["0.34","0.05","0.61","1.00"],"answer":0,"explanation":"With q as the recessive-allele frequency, p=1−q and heterozygotes occur at 2pq.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1106","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"If a producer stores 18,500 kJ of chemical energy and approximately 10% is transferred to the next trophic level, how much energy is available there?","options":["1,850 kJ","185 kJ","9,250 kJ","17,500 kJ"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Using the ecological efficiency approximation, 10% of the energy is transferred to the next trophic level.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1107","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"In a cross between two heterozygous plants with alleles Q and q, where Q is dominant for quiet and q is recessive for loud, what proportion of offspring is expected to show loud?","options":["25%","50%","75%","100%"],"answer":0,"explanation":"A heterozygous × heterozygous cross gives a 1:2:1 genotype ratio and therefore 25% recessive phenotype.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1109","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A plant transpires at an average rate of 5 cm³ of water per hour for 7 hours. How much water is lost in that period?","options":["35 cm³","12 cm³","0.71 cm³","40 cm³"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Total water loss = rate × time.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1110","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"In a healthy adult, alveolar oxygen partial pressure is 121 mmHg while venous blood oxygen partial pressure is 35 mmHg. Which gas will diffuse from the alveolus into the blood?","options":["Oxygen","Carbon dioxide","Nitrogen","Water vapour"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Oxygen moves down its partial-pressure gradient from alveolar air into venous blood.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"crea