 is recessive for drooping, what proportion of offspring is expected to show drooping?","options":["25%","50%","75%","100%"],"answer":0,"explanation":"A heterozygous × heterozygous cross gives a 1:2:1 genotype ratio and therefore 25% recessive phenotype.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1123","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A plant transpires at an average rate of 6 cm³ of water per hour for 8 hours. How much water is lost in that period?","options":["48 cm³","14 cm³","0.75 cm³","54 cm³"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Total water loss = rate × time.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1124","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"In a healthy adult, alveolar oxygen partial pressure is 123 mmHg while venous blood oxygen partial pressure is 36 mmHg. Which gas will diffuse from the alveolus into the blood?","options":["Oxygen","Carbon dioxide","Nitrogen","Water vapour"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Oxygen moves down its partial-pressure gradient from alveolar air into venous blood.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1127","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which process most directly contributes to genetic variation by metaphase I?","options":["independent assortment","binary fission","mitosis","cytokinesis"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Independent assortment contributes to genetic variation in the stated context.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1128","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A population contains 3900 organisms. In one year there are 253 births, 146 deaths, 87 immigrants and 58 emigrants. What is the net increase?","options":["136","107","29","146"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Net population change = births − deaths + immigration − emigration.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1129","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which hormone is most directly associated with the following physiological effect: support gamete development?","options":["FSH","insulin","thyroxine","ADH"],"answer":0,"explanation":"FSH has the stated physiological role.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1130","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which structure is best adapted to move mucus and trapped particles?","options":["cilia — move mucus and trapped particles","nephrons — filter blood and form urine","mitochondria — carry out aerobic respiration","guard cells — control stomatal opening"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Cilia is specialised for the stated function.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1131","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which option correctly matches alveoli with its principal role?","options":["alveoli — gas exchange","red blood cells — oxygen","muscle fibres — contraction","testes — sperm and testosterone"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The selected structure is correctly matched with its principal role.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1132","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"In a large randomly mating population, the frequency of an autosomal recessive allele is 0.24. Assuming Hardy–Weinberg conditions, what is the expected frequency of heterozygotes?","options":["0.36","0.06","0.58","1.00"],"answer":0,"explanation":"With q as the recessive-allele frequency, p=1−q and heterozygotes occur at 2pq.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1134","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"If a producer stores 19,500 kJ of chemical energy and approximately 10% is transferred to the next trophic level, how much energy is available there?","options":["1,950 kJ","195 kJ","9,750 kJ","18,500 kJ"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Using the ecological efficiency approximation, 10% of the energy is transferred to the next trophic level.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1135","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"In a cross between two heterozygous plants with alleles V and v, where V is dominant for violet and v is recessive for white, what proportion of offspring is expected to show white?","options":["25%","50%","75%","100%"],"answer":0,"explanation":"A heterozygous × heterozygous cross gives a 1:2:1 genotype ratio and therefore 25% recessive phenotype.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1137","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A plant transpires at an average rate of 2 cm³ of water per hour for 9 hours. How much water is lost in that period?","options":["18 cm³","11 cm³","0.22 cm³","20 cm³"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Total water loss = rate × time.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1138","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"In a healthy adult, alveolar oxygen partial pressure is 125 mmHg while venous blood oxygen partial pressure is 37 mmHg. Which gas will diffuse from the alveolus into the blood?","options":["Oxygen","Carbon dioxide","Nitrogen","Water vapour"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Oxygen moves down its partial-pressure gradient from alveolar air into venous blood.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1141","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which process most directly contributes to genetic variation by fusion of gametes?","options":["random fertilisation","binary fission","mitosis","cytokinesis"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Random fertilisation contributes to genetic variation in the stated context.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1142","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A population contains 4000 organisms. In one year there are 260 births, 150 deaths, 90 immigrants and 60 emigrants. What is the net increase?","options":["140","110","30","150"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Net population change = births − deaths + immigration − emigration.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1143","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which hormone is most directly associated with the following physiological effect: stimulate testosterone secretion in males?","options":["LH","insulin","thyroxine","ADH"],"answer":0,"explanation":"LH has the stated physiological role.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1145","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which structure is best adapted to increase absorptive surface area?","options":["microvilli — increase absorptive surface area","stomata — regulate gaseous exchange and water loss","ribosomes — synthesise proteins","myelin sheath — speed up impulse conduction"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Microvilli is specialised for the stated function.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1146","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which option correctly matches stomata with its principal role?","options":["stomata — gaseous exchange","white blood cells — immune defence","palisade cells — photosynthesis","kidneys — excretion and osmoregulation"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The selected structure is correctly matched with its principal role.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1148","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"In a large randomly mating population, the frequency of an autosomal recessive allele is 0.25. Assuming Hardy–Weinberg conditions, what is the expected frequency of heterozygotes?","options":["0.38","0.06","0.56","1.00"],"answer":0,"explanation":"With q as the recessive-allele frequency, p=1−q and heterozygotes occur at 2pq.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1149","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"If a producer stores 20,000 kJ of chemical energy and approximately 10% is transferred to the next trophic level, how much energy is available there?","options":["2,000 kJ","200 kJ","10,000 kJ","19,000 kJ"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Using the ecological efficiency approximation, 10% of the energy is transferred to the next trophic level.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false}],"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z"}],"announcements":[{"id":"ann-welcome-2026","title":"Welcome to the Gifted Brainz 2026 Learning Hub","body":"<p>Welcome to the updated Gifted Brainz Tutorial learning hub. Your five core subjects now have structured learning materials, a core question bank and a subject mock CBT.</p><p>Use <b>Learning Materials</b> to study a topic first, then use <b>Question Bank</b> for practice and corrections.</p>","format":"html","bodyFormat":"html","attachments":[],"media":[],"published":true,"audience":"students","createdAt":"2026-08-11T00:00:00.000Z","date":"2026-08-11T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"ann-study-cycle","title":"Recommended Study Cycle","body":"<p>For each topic, follow this four-step cycle: <b>Learn → Practise → Review → Re-attempt</b>. Read the lesson note, answer questions without guessing, study every correction, and then repeat missed items.</p>","format":"html","bodyFormat":"html","attachments":[],"media":[],"published":true,"audience":"students","createdAt":"2026-08-11T00:00:00.000Z","date":"2026-08-11T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"ann-cbt-guidance","title":"CBT Practice Guidance","body":"<p>Mock CBTs are timed. Question Bank <b>Study Mode</b> gives immediate feedback, while <b>Practice Mode</b> keeps answers hidden until submission.</p><p>After every attempt, read the correction and explanation rather than focusing only on the percentage score.</p>","format":"html","bodyFormat":"html","attachments":[],"media":[],"published":true,"audience":"students","createdAt":"2026-08-11T00:00:00.000Z","date":"2026-08-11T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"ann-content-release","title":"Content Pack v1 — Five Subjects Live","body":"<p>The first content-complete curriculum pack is now available across Mathematics, Use of English, Physics, Chemistry and Biology.</p><ul><li>25 structured learning materials</li><li>150 question-bank items</li><li>5 subject mock CBTs</li><li>Corrections and explanations for every seeded question</li></ul>","format":"html","bodyFormat":"html","attachments":[],"media":[],"published":true,"audience":"students","createdAt":"2026-08-11T00:00:00.000Z","date":"2026-08-11T00:00:00.000Z"}],"results":[],"registrationCodes":[],"questionBank":[{"id":"qb-mathematics-01","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A trader buys an article for ₦8,000 and spends ₦6,000 on transport. He then sells it for ₦15,000. What is the percentage profit on the total cost?","options":["7.14%","87.50%","6.67%","0.01%"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Total cost = purchase price + transport. Percentage profit = profit ÷ total cost × 100.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-mathematics-02","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"If x² -7x +12 = 0, what is the sum of the squares of its roots?","options":["25","49","12","27"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The roots are r₁ and r₂. Their squared sum is r₁²+r₂²=(r₁+r₂)²−2r₁r₂.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-mathematics-03","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"An arithmetic progression has first term 4 and common difference 3. What is its 9th term?","options":["28","31","25","63"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Use Tₙ = a + (n−1)d.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-mathematics-04","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Simplify 3^4 × 3^3.","options":["2187","531441","3","16384"],"answer":0,"explanation":"For equal bases, indices are added when multiplying powers.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-mathematics-05","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A sector has radius 5 cm and central angle 75°. What is its area in terms of π?","options":["125/24π cm²","25π cm²","125/12π cm²","120π cm²"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Sector area = θ/360 × πr².","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-mathematics-06","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Solve simultaneously: 3x + 2y = 17 and 2x + 3y = 18. What is the value of x?","options":["3","4","2","5"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Use elimination or substitution; the simultaneous equations give x as the stated value.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-mathematics-07","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A box contains 4 red and 5 blue counters. Two counters are drawn without replacement. What is the probability that both are red?","options":["1/6","4/9","5/18","8/9"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Multiply the probability of drawing a red first by the probability of drawing a red second without replacement.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-mathematics-08","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Four test scores have mean 51. Three scores are 45, 55 and 48. What is the fourth score?","options":["56","51","59","53"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The total of four scores is 4×mean; subtract the three known scores.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-mathematics-09","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A circular tank has radius 4 cm. What is the ratio of its circumference to its area?","options":["2/4","1/4","4/2","2/5"],"answer":0,"explanation":"C/A = 2πr ÷ πr² = 2/r.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-mathematics-10","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Find the square of the distance between (2, 3) and (6, 8).","options":["41","9","20","43"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Use d²=(x₂−x₁)²+(y₂−y₁)².","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-mathematics-11","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A trader buys an article for ₦9,000 and spends ₦7,000 on transport. He then sells it for ₦17,000. What is the percentage profit on the total cost?","options":["6.25%","88.89%","5.88%","0.01%"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Total cost = purchase price + transport. Percentage profit = profit ÷ total cost × 100.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-mathematics-12","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"If x² -9x +20 = 0, what is the sum of the squares of its roots?","options":["41","81","20","43"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The roots are r₁ and r₂. Their squared sum is r₁²+r₂²=(r₁+r₂)²−2r₁r₂.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-mathematics-13","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"An arithmetic progression has first term 5 and common difference 4. What is its 10th term?","options":["41","45","37","90"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Use Tₙ = a + (n−1)d.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-mathematics-14","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Simplify 4^5 × 4^4.","options":["262144","1099511627776","4","1953125"],"answer":0,"explanation":"For equal bases, indices are added when multiplying powers.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-mathematics-15","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A sector has radius 6 cm and central angle 90°. What is its area in terms of π?","options":["9π cm²","36π cm²","18π cm²","144π cm²"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Sector area = θ/360 × πr².","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-mathematics-16","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Solve simultaneously: 4x + 3y = 31 and 3x + 4y = 32. What is the value of x?","options":["4","5","3","6"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Use elimination or substitution; the simultaneous equations give x as the stated value.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-mathematics-17","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A box contains 5 red and 6 blue counters. Two counters are drawn without replacement. What is the probability that both are red?","options":["2/11","5/11","3/11","10/11"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Multiply the probability of drawing a red first by the probability of drawing a red second without replacement.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-mathematics-18","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Four test scores have mean 52. Three scores are 46, 56 and 49. What is the fourth score?","options":["57","52","60","54"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The total of four scores is 4×mean; subtract the three known scores.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-mathematics-19","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A circular tank has radius 5 cm. What is the ratio of its circumference to its area?","options":["2/5","1/5","5/2","2/6"],"answer":0,"explanation":"C/A = 2πr ÷ πr² = 2/r.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-mathematics-20","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Find the square of the distance between (3, 4) and (8, 10).","options":["61","11","30","63"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Use d²=(x₂−x₁)²+(y₂−y₁)².","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-mathematics-21","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A trader buys an article for ₦10,000 and spends ₦8,000 on transport. He then sells it for ₦19,000. What is the percentage profit on the total cost?","options":["5.56%","90.00%","5.26%","0.01%"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Total cost = purchase price + transport. Percentage profit = profit ÷ total cost × 100.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-mathematics-22","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"If x² -11x +30 = 0, what is the sum of the squares of its roots?","options":["61","121","30","63"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The roots are r₁ and r₂. Their squared sum is r₁²+r₂²=(r₁+r₂)²−2r₁r₂.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-mathematics-23","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"An arithmetic progression has first term 6 and common difference 5. What is its 11th term?","options":["56","61","51","121"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Use Tₙ = a + (n−1)d.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-mathematics-24","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Simplify 5^6 × 5^5.","options":["48828125","931322574615478515625","5","362797056"],"answer":0,"explanation":"For equal bases, indices are added when multiplying powers.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-mathematics-25","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A sector has radius 7 cm and central angle 105°. What is its area in terms of π?","options":["343/24π cm²","49π cm²","343/12π cm²","168π cm²"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Sector area = θ/360 × πr².","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-mathematics-26","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Solve simultaneously: 5x + 4y = 49 and 4x + 5y = 50. What is the value of x?","options":["5","6","4","7"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Use elimination or substitution; the simultaneous equations give x as the stated value.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-mathematics-27","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A box contains 6 red and 7 blue counters. Two counters are drawn without replacement. What is the probability that both are red?","options":["5/26","6/13","7/26","12/13"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Multiply the probability of drawing a red first by the probability of drawing a red second without replacement.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-mathematics-28","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Four test scores have mean 53. Three scores are 47, 57 and 50. What is the fourth score?","options":["58","53","61","55"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The total of four scores is 4×mean; subtract the three known scores.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-mathematics-29","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A circular tank has radius 6 cm. What is the ratio of its circumference to its area?","options":["2/6","1/6","6/2","2/7"],"answer":0,"explanation":"C/A = 2πr ÷ πr² = 2/r.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-mathematics-30","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Find the square of the distance between (4, 5) and (10, 12).","options":["85","13","42","87"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Use d²=(x₂−x₁)²+(y₂−y₁)².","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-math-gen-001","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A trader buys an article for ₦11,000 and spends ₦9,000 on transport. He then sells it for ₦21,000. What is the percentage profit on the total cost?","options":["5.00%","90.91%","4.76%","0.01%"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Total cost = purchase price + transport. Percentage profit = profit ÷ total cost × 100.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-math-gen-002","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"If x² -13x +42 = 0, what is the sum of the squares of its roots?","options":["85","169","42","87"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The roots are r₁ and r₂. Their squared sum is r₁²+r₂²=(r₁+r₂)²−2r₁r₂.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-math-gen-003","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"An arithmetic progression has first term 7 and common difference 6. What is its 12th term?","options":["73","79","67","156"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Use Tₙ = a + (n−1)d.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-math-gen-004","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Simplify 6^7 × 6^2.","options":["10077696","78364164096","7776","40353607"],"answer":0,"explanation":"For equal bases, indices are added when multiplying powers.",