":"Four test scores have mean 66. Three scores are 60, 70 and 63. What is the fourth score?","options":["71","66","74","68"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The total of four scores is 4×mean; subtract the three known scores.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-math-gen-150","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A circular tank has radius 19 cm. What is the ratio of its circumference to its area?","options":["2/19","1/19","19/2","2/20"],"answer":0,"explanation":"C/A = 2πr ÷ πr² = 2/r.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-math-gen-151","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Find the square of the distance between (3, 2) and (6, 7).","options":["34","8","15","36"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Use d²=(x₂−x₁)²+(y₂−y₁)².","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-math-gen-152","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A trader buys an article for ₦24,000 and spends ₦22,000 on transport. He then sells it for ₦47,000. What is the percentage profit on the total cost?","options":["2.17%","95.83%","2.13%","0.00%"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Total cost = purchase price + transport. Percentage profit = profit ÷ total cost × 100.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-math-gen-153","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"If x² -39x +380 = 0, what is the sum of the squares of its roots?","options":["761","1521","380","763"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The roots are r₁ and r₂. Their squared sum is r₁²+r₂²=(r₁+r₂)²−2r₁r₂.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-math-gen-154","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"An arithmetic progression has first term 20 and common difference 5. What is its 25th term?","options":["140","145","135","625"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Use Tₙ = a + (n−1)d.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-math-gen-157","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Simplify 19^5 × 19^3.","options":["16983563041","15181127029874798299","361","25600000000"],"answer":0,"explanation":"For equal bases, indices are added when multiplying powers.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-math-gen-158","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A sector has radius 21 cm and central angle 90°. What is its area in terms of π?","options":["441/4π cm²","441π cm²","441/2π cm²","1764π cm²"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Sector area = θ/360 × πr².","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-math-gen-159","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Solve simultaneously: 4x + 6y = 196 and 6x + 4y = 194. What is the value of x?","options":["19","20","18","21"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Use elimination or substitution; the simultaneous equations give x as the stated value.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-math-gen-160","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A box contains 20 red and 21 blue counters. Two counters are drawn without replacement. What is the probability that both are red?","options":["19/82","20/41","21/82","40/41"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Multiply the probability of drawing a red first by the probability of drawing a red second without replacement.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-math-gen-161","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Four test scores have mean 67. Three scores are 61, 71 and 64. What is the fourth score?","options":["72","67","75","69"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The total of four scores is 4×mean; subtract the three known scores.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-math-gen-162","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A circular tank has radius 20 cm. What is the ratio of its circumference to its area?","options":["2/20","1/20","20/2","2/21"],"answer":0,"explanation":"C/A = 2πr ÷ πr² = 2/r.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-math-gen-163","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Find the square of the distance between (4, 3) and (8, 9).","options":["52","10","24","54"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Use d²=(x₂−x₁)²+(y₂−y₁)².","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-math-gen-164","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A trader buys an article for ₦25,000 and spends ₦23,000 on transport. He then sells it for ₦49,000. What is the percentage profit on the total cost?","options":["2.08%","96.00%","2.04%","0.00%"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Total cost = purchase price + transport. Percentage profit = profit ÷ total cost × 100.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-math-gen-165","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"If x² -41x +420 = 0, what is the sum of the squares of its roots?","options":["841","1681","420","843"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The roots are r₁ and r₂. Their squared sum is r₁²+r₂²=(r₁+r₂)²−2r₁r₂.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-math-gen-166","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"An arithmetic progression has first term 21 and common difference 6. What is its 26th term?","options":["171","177","165","702"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Use Tₙ = a + (n−1)d.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-math-gen-169","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Simplify 20^6 × 20^4.","options":["10240000000000","16777216000000000000000000000000","400","16679880978201"],"answer":0,"explanation":"For equal bases, indices are added when multiplying powers.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-math-gen-170","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A sector has radius 22 cm and central angle 105°. What is its area in terms of π?","options":["847/6π cm²","484π cm²","847/3π cm²","11616/7π cm²"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Sector area = θ/360 × πr².","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-mathematics-gen-1000","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Solve simultaneously: 5x + 1y = 121 and 1x + 5y = 125. What is the value of x?","options":["20","21","19","22"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Use elimination or substitution; the simultaneous equations give x as the stated value.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-mathematics-gen-1001","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A box contains 21 red and 22 blue counters. Two counters are drawn without replacement. What is the probability that both are red?","options":["10/43","21/43","11/43","42/43"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Multiply the probability of drawing a red first by the probability of drawing a red second without replacement.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-mathematics-gen-1002","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Four test scores have mean 68. Three scores are 62, 72 and 65. What is the fourth score?","options":["73","68","76","70"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The total of four scores is 4×mean; subtract the three known scores.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-mathematics-gen-1003","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A circular tank has radius 21 cm. What is the ratio of its circumference to its area?","options":["2/21","1/21","21/2","2/22"],"answer":0,"explanation":"C/A = 2πr ÷ πr² = 2/r.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-mathematics-gen-1004","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Find the square of the distance between (5, 4) and (10, 11).","options":["74","12","35","76"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Use d²=(x₂−x₁)²+(y₂−y₁)².","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-mathematics-gen-1005","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A trader buys an article for ₦26,000 and spends ₦24,000 on transport. He then sells it for ₦51,000. What is the percentage profit on the total cost?","options":["2.00%","96.15%","1.96%","0.00%"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Total cost = purchase price + transport. Percentage profit = profit ÷ total cost × 100.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-mathematics-gen-1006","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"If x² -43x +462 = 0, what is the sum of the squares of its roots?","options":["925","1849","462","927"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The roots are r₁ and r₂. Their squared sum is r₁²+r₂²=(r₁+r₂)²−2r₁r₂.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-mathematics-gen-1007","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"An arithmetic progression has first term 22 and common difference 7. What is its 27th term?","options":["204","211","197","783"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Use Tₙ = a + (n−1)d.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-mathematics-gen-1008","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Simplify 21^7 × 21^5.","options":["7355827511386641","18952884486433699020098042171468383867092598701","441","12855002631049216"],"answer":0,"explanation":"For equal ba