e":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-mathematics-gen-1013","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A circular tank has radius 22 cm. What is the ratio of its circumference to its area?","options":["2/22","1/22","22/2","2/23"],"answer":0,"explanation":"C/A = 2πr ÷ πr² = 2/r.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-mathematics-gen-1014","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Find the square of the distance between (6, 5) and (12, 13).","options":["100","14","48","102"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Use d²=(x₂−x₁)²+(y₂−y₁)².","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-mathematics-gen-1015","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A trader buys an article for ₦27,000 and spends ₦25,000 on transport. He then sells it for ₦53,000. What is the percentage profit on the total cost?","options":["1.92%","96.30%","1.89%","0.00%"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Total cost = purchase price + transport. Percentage profit = profit ÷ total cost × 100.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-mathematics-gen-1016","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"If x² -45x +506 = 0, what is the sum of the squares of its roots?","options":["1013","2025","506","1015"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The roots are r₁ and r₂. Their squared sum is r₁²+r₂²=(r₁+r₂)²−2r₁r₂.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-mathematics-gen-1017","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"An arithmetic progression has first term 23 and common difference 8. What is its 28th term?","options":["239","247","231","868"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Use Tₙ = a + (n−1)d.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-mathematics-gen-1018","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Simplify 22^3 × 22^2.","options":["5153632","113379904","22","6436343"],"answer":0,"explanation":"For equal bases, indices are added when multiplying powers.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-mathematics-gen-1019","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A sector has radius 24 cm and central angle 60°. What is its area in terms of π?","options":["96π cm²","576π cm²","192π cm²","3456π cm²"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Sector area = θ/360 × πr².","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-mathematics-gen-1020","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Solve simultaneously: 2x + 3y = 113 and 3x + 2y = 112. What is the value of x?","options":["22","23","21","24"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Use elimination or substitution; the simultaneous equations give x as the stated value.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-mathematics-gen-1021","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A box contains 23 red and 24 blue counters. Two counters are drawn without replacement. What is the probability that both are red?","options":["11/47","23/47","12/47","46/47"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Multiply the probability of drawing a red first by the probability of drawing a red second without replacement.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-mathematics-gen-1022","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Four test scores have mean 70. Three scores are 64, 74 and 67. What is the fourth score?","options":["75","70","78","72"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The total of four scores is 4×mean; subtract the three known scores.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-mathematics-gen-1023","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A circular tank has radius 23 cm. What is the ratio of its circumference to its area?","options":["2/23","1/23","23/2","2/24"],"answer":0,"explanation":"C/A = 2πr ÷ πr² = 2/r.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-mathematics-gen-1024","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Find the square of the distance between (7, 6) and (10, 10).","options":["25","7","12","27"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Use d²=(x₂−x₁)²+(y₂−y₁)².","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Mathematics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-physics-roman-clean-001","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about a 2 kg body moving on a straight track are correct?\n\nI. If the resultant force is non-zero, its velocity changes.\nII. If the resultant force is zero, the body may still move at constant velocity.\nIII. For a given mass, doubling the resultant force doubles the acceleration.\nIV. Acceleration is measured in newtons.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; acceleration is measured in m/s², while the newton is a unit of force.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":true},{"id":"qb-physics-roman-clean-021","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about a circuit containing a 5 Ω resistor carrying 4 A are correct?\n\nI. The potential difference across the resistor is 20 V.\nII. The electrical power is 80 W.\nIII. Ohm’s law gives V=IR for an ohmic resistor at constant physical conditions.\nIV. The resistance is found by multiplying voltage by current.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; resistance is R=V/I, not VI.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":true},{"id":"qb-physics-roman-clean-002","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about a wave of frequency 8 Hz and wavelength 0.29 m are correct?\n\nI. Its speed is fλ.\nII. Its period is 1/f.\nIII. If frequency increases while wavelength remains fixed, speed increases.\nIV. Frequency is measured in metres.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; frequency is measured in hertz.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":true},{"id":"qb-physics-roman-clean-022","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about a 7 kg object raised through 8 m are correct, taking g=10 m/s²?\n\nI. Its gravitational potential energy increases by mgh.\nII. The increase is 560 J.\nIII. Raising it higher increases its gravitational potential energy.\nIV. Gravitational potential energy is measured in watts.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; energy is measured in joules, while the watt is a unit of power.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":true},{"id":"qb-physics-roman-clean-003","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about a 6 kg body moving on a straight track are correct?\n\nI. If the resultant force is non-zero, its velocity changes.\nII. If the resultant force is zero, the body may still move at constant velocity.\nIII. For a given mass, doubling the resultant force doubles the acceleration.\nIV. Acceleration is measured in newtons.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; acceleration is measured in m/s², while the newton is a unit of force.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":true},{"id":"qb-physics-roman-clean-023","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about a circuit containing a 9 Ω resistor carrying 3 A are correct?\n\nI. The potential difference across the resistor is 27 V.\nII. The electrical power is 81 W.\nIII. Ohm’s law gives V=IR for an ohmic resistor at constant physical conditions.\nIV. The resistance is found by multiplying voltage by current.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; resistance is R=V/I, not VI.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":true},{"id":"qb-physics-roman-clean-004","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about a wave of frequency 12 Hz and wavelength 0.33 m are correct?\n\nI. Its speed is fλ.\nII. Its period is 1/f.\nIII. If frequency increases while wavelength remains fixed, speed increases.\nIV. Frequency is measured in metres.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; frequency is measured in hertz.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":true},{"id":"qb-physics-roman-clean-024","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about a 11 kg object raised through 5 m are correct, taking g=10 m/s²?\n\nI. Its gravitational potential energy increases by mgh.\nII. The increase is 550 J.\nIII. Raising it higher increases its gravitational potential energy.\nIV. Gravitational potential energy is measured in watts.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; energy is measured in joules, while the watt is a unit of power.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":true},{"id":"qb-physics-01","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"How much heat is needed to raise the temperature of 3 kg of water by 6 °C? Take c=4200 J kg⁻¹ °C⁻¹.","options":["75,600 J","12,600 J","25,200 J","7,560.0 J"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Heat supplied Q=mcΔT.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-physics-02","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Light of wavelength 340 nm falls on a surface. Using h=6.63×10⁻³⁴ J s and c=3.0×10⁸ m/s, what is the energy of one photon?","options":["5.850e-19 J","7.514e-49 J","2.925e-19 J","6.763e-32 J"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Photon energy is E=hc/λ.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-physics-03","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A car travels with initial speed 10 m/s and uniform acceleration 4 m/s² for 5 s. What distance does it cover?","options":["100 m","50 m","150 m","Insufficient information to determine the answer"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Use s = ut + ½at².","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-physics-04","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A 4 kg object is acted upon by a resultant force of 20 N. What acceleration does it acquire?","options":["5 m/s²","20 m/s²","4 m/s²","6 m/s²"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Newton’s second law gives a=F/m.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-physics-05","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A load of mass 5 kg is lifted vertically through 6 m. Taking g=10 m/s², what increase in gravitational potential energy occurs?","options":["300 J","30 J","50 J","150 J"],"answer":0,"explanation":"ΔPE=mgh.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-physics-06","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A 4 kg trolley increases its speed from 6 m/s to 13 m/s. What impulse acts on it?","options":["28 N s","52 N s","24 N s","76 N s"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Impulse equals change in momentum: m(v−u).","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-physics-07","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A resistor of 5 Ω carries a current of 4 A. What electrical power is dissipated?","options":["80 W","20 W","9 W","1.25 W"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Power P=I²R or VI.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-physics-08","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A wave has frequency 7 Hz and wavelength 0.3 m. Calculate its speed.","options":["2.1 m/s","23.3333 m/s","7.3 m/s","0.0428571 m/s"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Wave speed v=fλ.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-physics-09","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A 3 kg object moves at 6 m/s in a circle of radius 4 m. What is the magnitude of its centripetal force?","options":["27 N","4.5 N","72 N","432 N"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Centripetal force is mv²/r.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-physics-10","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A converging lens has focal length 0.14 m and forms a real image when an object is 0.4 m from it. What is the image distance?","options":["0.215 m","0.104 m","0.260 m","0.056 m"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Use the lens formula 1/f=1/u+1/v with consistent sign conventions for magnitudes in this real-object case.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-physics-11","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"How much heat is needed to raise the temperature of 4 kg of water by 7 °C? Take c=4200 J kg⁻¹ °C⁻¹.","options":["117,600 J","16,800 J","29,400 J","11,760.0 J"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Heat supplied Q=mcΔT.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-physics-12","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Light of wavelength 360 nm falls on a surface. Using h=6.63×10⁻³⁴ J s and c=3.0×10⁸ m/s, what is the energy of one photon?","options":["5.525e-19 J","7.956e-49 J","2.762e-19 J","7.160e-32 J"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Photon energy is E=hc/λ.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-physics-13","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A car travels with initial speed 11 m/s and uniform acceleration 5 m/s² for 6 s. What distance does it cover?","options":["156 m","66 m","246 m","90 m"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Use s = ut + ½at².","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-physics-14","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A 5 kg object is acted upon by a resultant force of 30 N. What acceleration does it acquire?","options":["6 m/s²","30 m/s²","5 m/s²","7 m/s²"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Newton’s second law gives a=F/m.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-physics-15","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A load of mass 6 kg is lifted vertically through 7 m. Taking g=10 m/s², what increase in gravitational potential energy occurs?","options":["420 J","42 J","60 J","210 J"],"answer":0,"explanation":"ΔPE=mgh.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-physics-16","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A 5 kg trolley increases its speed from 7 m/s to 15 m/s. What impulse acts on it?","options":["40 N s","75 N s","35 N s","110 N s"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Impulse equals change in momentum: m(v−u).","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-physics-17","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A resistor of 6 Ω carries a current of 5 A. What electrical power is dissipated?","options":["150 W","30 W","11 W","1.2 W"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Power P=I²R or VI.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-physics-18","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A wave has frequency 8 Hz and wavelength 0.35 m. Calculate its speed.","options":["2.8 m/s","22.8571 m/s","8.35 m/s","0.04375 m/s"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Wave speed v=fλ.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-physics-19","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A 4 kg object moves at 7 m/s in a circle of radius 5 m. What is the magnitude of its centripetal force?","options":["39.2 N","5.6 N","140 N","980 N"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Centripetal force is mv²/r.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-physics-20","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A converging lens has focal length 0.16 m and forms a real image when an object is 0.45 m from it. What is the image distance?","options":["0.248 m","0.118 m","0.290 m","0.072 m"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Use the lens formula 1/f=1/u+1/v with consistent sign conventions for magnitudes in this real-object case.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-physics-21","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"How much heat is needed to raise the temperature of 5 kg of water by 8 °C? Take c=4200 J kg⁻¹ °C⁻¹.","options":["168,000 J","21,000 J","33,600 J","16,800.0 J"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Heat supplied Q=mcΔT.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-physics-22","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Light of wavelength 380 nm falls on a surface. Using h=6.63×10⁻³⁴ J s and c=3.0×10⁸ m/s, what is the energy of one photon?","options":["5.234e-19 J","8.398e-49 J","2.617e-19 J","7.558e-32 J"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Photon energy is E=hc/λ.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-physics-23","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A car travels with initial speed 12 m/s and uniform acceleration 6 m/s² for 7 s. What distance does it cover?","options":["231 m","84 m","378 m","147 m"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Use s = ut + ½at².","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-physics-24","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A 6 kg object is acted upon by a resultant force of 42 N. What acceleration does it acquire?","options":["7 m/s²","42 m/s²","6 m/s