g object moves at 8 m/s in a circle of radius 6 m. What is the magnitude of its centripetal force?","options":["53.3333 N","6.66667 N","240 N","1920 N"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Centripetal force is mv²/r.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-physics-30","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A converging lens has focal length 0.18 m and forms a real image when an object is 0.5 m from it. What is the image distance?","options":["0.281 m","0.132 m","0.320 m","0.090 m"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Use the lens formula 1/f=1/u+1/v with consistent sign conventions for magnitudes in this real-object case.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-001","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"How much heat is needed to raise the temperature of 6 kg of water by 9 °C? Take c=4200 J kg⁻¹ °C⁻¹.","options":["226,800 J","25,200 J","37,800 J","22,680.0 J"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Heat supplied Q=mcΔT.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-002","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Light of wavelength 400 nm falls on a surface. Using h=6.63×10⁻³⁴ J s and c=3.0×10⁸ m/s, what is the energy of one photon?","options":["4.972e-19 J","8.840e-49 J","2.486e-19 J","7.956e-32 J"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Photon energy is E=hc/λ.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-physics-roman-clean-005","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about a 42 kg body moving on a straight track are correct?\n\nI. If the resultant force is non-zero, its velocity changes.\nII. If the resultant force is zero, the body may still move at constant velocity.\nIII. For a given mass, doubling the resultant force doubles the acceleration.\nIV. Acceleration is measured in newtons.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; acceleration is measured in m/s², while the newton is a unit of force.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":true},{"id":"qb-physics-roman-clean-025","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about a circuit containing a 45 Ω resistor carrying 4 A are correct?\n\nI. The potential difference across the resistor is 180 V.\nII. The electrical power is 720 W.\nIII. Ohm’s law gives V=IR for an ohmic resistor at constant physical conditions.\nIV. The resistance is found by multiplying voltage by current.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; resistance is R=V/I, not VI.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":true},{"id":"qb-physics-roman-clean-006","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about a wave of frequency 48 Hz and wavelength 0.69 m are correct?\n\nI. Its speed is fλ.\nII. Its period is 1/f.\nIII. If frequency increases while wavelength remains fixed, speed increases.\nIV. Frequency is measured in metres.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; frequency is measured in hertz.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":true},{"id":"qb-physics-roman-clean-026","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about a 47 kg object raised through 6 m are correct, taking g=10 m/s²?\n\nI. Its gravitational potential energy increases by mgh.\nII. The increase is 2820 J.\nIII. Raising it higher increases its gravitational potential energy.\nIV. Gravitational potential energy is measured in watts.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; energy is measured in joules, while the watt is a unit of power.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":true},{"id":"qb-physics-roman-clean-007","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about a 46 kg body moving on a straight track are correct?\n\nI. If the resultant force is non-zero, its velocity changes.\nII. If the resultant force is zero, the body may still move at constant velocity.\nIII. For a given mass, doubling the resultant force doubles the acceleration.\nIV. Acceleration is measured in newtons.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; acceleration is measured in m/s², while the newton is a unit of force.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":true},{"id":"qb-physics-roman-clean-027","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about a circuit containing a 49 Ω resistor carrying 3 A are correct?\n\nI. The potential difference across the resistor is 147 V.\nII. The electrical power is 441 W.\nIII. Ohm’s law gives V=IR for an ohmic resistor at constant physical conditions.\nIV. The resistance is found by multiplying voltage by current.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; resistance is R=V/I, not VI.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":true},{"id":"qb-physics-roman-clean-008","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about a wave of frequency 52 Hz and wavelength 0.73 m are correct?\n\nI. Its speed is fλ.\nII. Its period is 1/f.\nIII. If frequency increases while wavelength remains fixed, speed increases.\nIV. Frequency is measured in metres.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; frequency is measured in hertz.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":true},{"id":"qb-physics-roman-clean-028","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about a 51 kg object raised through 3 m are correct, taking g=10 m/s²?\n\nI. Its gravitational potential energy increases by mgh.\nII. The increase is 1530 J.\nIII. Raising it higher increases its gravitational potential energy.\nIV. Gravitational potential energy is measured in watts.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; energy is measured in joules, while the watt is a unit of power.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":true},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-003","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"How much heat is needed to raise the temperature of 7 kg of water by 10 °C? Take c=4200 J kg⁻¹ °C⁻¹.","options":["294,000 J","29,400 J","42,000 J","29,400.0 J"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Heat supplied Q=mcΔT.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-004","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Light of wavelength 420 nm falls on a surface. Using h=6.63×10⁻³⁴ J s and c=3.0×10⁸ m/s, what is the energy of one photon?","options":["4.736e-19 J","9.282e-49 J","2.368e-19 J","8.354e-32 J"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Photon energy is E=hc/λ.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-005","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A car travels with initial speed 14 m/s and uniform acceleration 3 m/s² for 3 s. What distance does it cover?","options":["55.5 m","42 m","69 m","13.5 m"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Use s = ut + ½at².","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-006","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A 8 kg object is acted upon by a resultant force of 24 N. What acceleration does it acquire?","options":["3 m/s²","24 m/s²","8 m/s²","4 m/s²"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Newton’s second law gives a=F/m.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-007","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A load of mass 9 kg is lifted vertically through 10 m. Taking g=10 m/s², what increase in gravitational potential energy occurs?","options":["900 J","90 J","450 J","Insufficient information to determine the answer"],"answer":0,"explanation":"ΔPE=mgh.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-008","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A 8 kg trolley increases its speed from 10 m/s to 16 m/s. What impulse acts on it?","options":["48 N s","128 N s","80 N s","208 N s"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Impulse equals change in momentum: m(v−u).","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-009","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A resistor of 9 Ω carries a current of 8 A. What electrical power is dissipated?","options":["576 W","72 W","17 W","1.125 W"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Power P=I²R or VI.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-010","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A wave has frequency 11 Hz and wavelength 0.5 m. Calculate its speed.","options":["5.5 m/s","22 m/s","11.5 m/s","0.0454545 m/s"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Wave speed v=fλ.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-011","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A 2 kg object moves at 10 m/s in a circle of radius 8 m. What is the magnitude of its centripetal force?","options":["25 N","2.5 N","160 N","1600 N"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Centripetal force is mv²/r.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-012","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A converging lens has focal length 0.22 m and forms a real image when an object is 0.6 m from it. What is the image distance?","options":["0.347 m","0.161 m","0.380 m","0.132 m"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Use the lens formula 1/f=1/u+1/v with consistent sign conventions for magnitudes in this real-object case.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-013","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"How much heat is needed to raise the temperature of 8 kg of water by 11 °C? Take c=4200 J kg⁻¹ °C⁻¹.","options":["369,600 J","33,600 J","46,200 J","36,960.0 J"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Heat supplied Q=mcΔT.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-014","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Light of wavelength 440 nm falls on a surface. Using h=6.63×10⁻³⁴ J s and c=3.0×10⁸ m/s, what is the energy of one photon?","options":["4.520e-19 J","9.724e-49 J","2.260e-19 J","8.752e-32 J"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Photon energy is E=hc/λ.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-015","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A car travels with initial speed 15 m/s and uniform acceleration 4 m/s² for 4 s. What distance does it cover?","options":["92 m","60 m","124 m","32 m"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Use s = ut + ½at².","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-016","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A 9 kg object is acted upon by a resultant force of 36 N. What acceleration does it acquire?","options":["4 m/s²","36 m/s²","9 m/s²","5 m/s²"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Newton’s second law gives a=F/m.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-017","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A load of mass 10 kg is lifted vertically through 11 m. Taking g=10 m/s², what increase in gravitational potential energy occurs?","options":["1100 J","110 J","100 J","550 J"],"answer":0,"explanation":"ΔPE=mgh.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-018","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A 9 kg trolley increases its speed from 11 m/s to 18 m/s. What impulse acts on it?","options":["63 N s","162 N s","99 N s","261 N s"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Impulse equals change in momentum: m(v−u).","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-019","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A resistor of 10 Ω carries a current of 9 A. What electrical power is dissipated?","options":["810 W","90 W","19 W","1.11111 W"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Power P=I²R or VI.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-020","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A wave has frequency 12 Hz and wavelength 0.55 m. Calculate its speed.","options":["6.6 m/s","21.8182 m/s","12.55 m/s","0.0458333 m/s"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Wave speed v=fλ.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-021","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A 3 kg object moves at 11 m/s in a circle of radius 9 m. What is the magnitude of its centripetal force?","options":["40.3333 N","3.66667 N","297 N","3267 N"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Centripetal force is mv²/r.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-022","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A converging lens has focal length 0.24 m and forms a real image when an object is 0.65 m from it. What is the image distance?","options":["0.380 m","0.175 m","0.410 m","0.156 m"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Use the lens formula 1/f=1/u+1/v with consistent sign conventions for magnitudes in this real-object case.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-023","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"How much heat is needed to raise the temperature of 9 kg of water by 12 °C? Take c=4200 J kg⁻¹ °C⁻¹.","options":["453,600 J","37,800 J","50,400 J","45,360.0 J"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Heat supplied Q=mcΔT.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-024","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Light of wavelength 460 nm falls on a surface. Using h=6.63×10⁻³⁴ J s and c=3.0×10⁸ m/s, what is the energy of one photon?","options":["4.324e-19 J","1.017e-48 J","2.162e-19 J","9.149e-32 J"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Photon energy is E=hc/λ.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-025","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A car travels with initial speed 16 m/s and uniform acceleration 5 m/s² for 5 s. What distance does it cover?","options":["142.5 m","80 m","205 m","62.5 m"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Use s = ut + ½at².",