ons":["1372 W","98 W","21 W","0.5 W"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Power P=I²R or VI.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-065","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A wave has frequency 17 Hz and wavelength 0.4 m. Calculate its speed.","options":["6.8 m/s","42.5 m/s","17.4 m/s","0.0235294 m/s"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Wave speed v=fλ.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-066","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A 3 kg object moves at 16 m/s in a circle of radius 14 m. What is the magnitude of its centripetal force?","options":["54.8571 N","3.42857 N","672 N","10752 N"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Centripetal force is mv²/r.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-067","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A converging lens has focal length 0.18 m and forms a real image when an object is 0.9 m from it. What is the image distance?","options":["0.225 m","0.150 m","0.720 m","0.162 m"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Use the lens formula 1/f=1/u+1/v with consistent sign conventions for magnitudes in this real-object case.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-068","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"How much heat is needed to raise the temperature of 14 kg of water by 9 °C? Take c=4200 J kg⁻¹ °C⁻¹.","options":["529,200 J","58,800 J","37,800 J","52,920.0 J"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Heat supplied Q=mcΔT.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-069","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Light of wavelength 560 nm falls on a surface. Using h=6.63×10⁻³⁴ J s and c=3.0×10⁸ m/s, what is the energy of one photon?","options":["3.552e-19 J","1.238e-48 J","1.776e-19 J","1.114e-31 J"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Photon energy is E=hc/λ.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-physics-roman-clean-013","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about a 122 kg body moving on a straight track are correct?\n\nI. If the resultant force is non-zero, its velocity changes.\nII. If the resultant force is zero, the body may still move at constant velocity.\nIII. For a given mass, doubling the resultant force doubles the acceleration.\nIV. Acceleration is measured in newtons.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; acceleration is measured in m/s², while the newton is a unit of force.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":true},{"id":"qb-physics-roman-clean-033","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about a circuit containing a 125 Ω resistor carrying 4 A are correct?\n\nI. The potential difference across the resistor is 500 V.\nII. The electrical power is 2000 W.\nIII. Ohm’s law gives V=IR for an ohmic resistor at constant physical conditions.\nIV. The resistance is found by multiplying voltage by current.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; resistance is R=V/I, not VI.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":true},{"id":"qb-physics-roman-clean-014","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about a wave of frequency 128 Hz and wavelength 1.49 m are correct?\n\nI. Its speed is fλ.\nII. Its period is 1/f.\nIII. If frequency increases while wavelength remains fixed, speed increases.\nIV. Frequency is measured in metres.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; frequency is measured in hertz.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":true},{"id":"qb-physics-roman-clean-034","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about a 127 kg object raised through 9 m are correct, taking g=10 m/s²?\n\nI. Its gravitational potential energy increases by mgh.\nII. The increase is 11430 J.\nIII. Raising it higher increases its gravitational potential energy.\nIV. Gravitational potential energy is measured in watts.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; energy is measured in joules, while the watt is a unit of power.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":true},{"id":"qb-physics-roman-clean-015","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about a 126 kg body moving on a straight track are correct?\n\nI. If the resultant force is non-zero, its velocity changes.\nII. If the resultant force is zero, the body may still move at constant velocity.\nIII. For a given mass, doubling the resultant force doubles the acceleration.\nIV. Acceleration is measured in newtons.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; acceleration is measured in m/s², while the newton is a unit of force.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":true},{"id":"qb-physics-roman-clean-035","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about a circuit containing a 129 Ω resistor carrying 3 A are correct?\n\nI. The potential difference across the resistor is 387 V.\nII. The electrical power is 1161 W.\nIII. Ohm’s law gives V=IR for an ohmic resistor at constant physical conditions.\nIV. The resistance is found by multiplying voltage by current.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; resistance is R=V/I, not VI.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":true},{"id":"qb-physics-roman-clean-016","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about a wave of frequency 132 Hz and wavelength 1.53 m are correct?\n\nI. Its speed is fλ.\nII. Its period is 1/f.\nIII. If frequency increases while wavelength remains fixed, speed increases.\nIV. Frequency is measured in metres.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; frequency is measured in hertz.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":true},{"id":"qb-physics-roman-clean-036","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about a 131 kg object raised through 6 m are correct, taking g=10 m/s²?\n\nI. Its gravitational potential energy increases by mgh.\nII. The increase is 7860 J.\nIII. Raising it higher increases its gravitational potential energy.\nIV. Gravitational potential energy is measured in watts.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; energy is measured in joules, while the watt is a unit of power.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":true},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-070","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"How much heat is needed to raise the temperature of 15 kg of water by 10 °C? Take c=4200 J kg⁻¹ °C⁻¹.","options":["630,000 J","63,000 J","42,000 J","63,000.0 J"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Heat supplied Q=mcΔT.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-071","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Light of wavelength 580 nm falls on a surface. Using h=6.63×10⁻³⁴ J s and c=3.0×10⁸ m/s, what is the energy of one photon?","options":["3.429e-19 J","1.282e-48 J","1.715e-19 J","1.154e-31 J"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Photon energy is E=hc/λ.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-072","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A car travels with initial speed 22 m/s and uniform acceleration 6 m/s² for 5 s. What distance does it cover?","options":["185 m","110 m","260 m","75 m"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Use s = ut + ½at².","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-073","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A 16 kg object is acted upon by a resultant force of 80 N. What acceleration does it acquire?","options":["5 m/s²","80 m/s²","16 m/s²","6 m/s²"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Newton’s second law gives a=F/m.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-074","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A load of mass 17 kg is lifted vertically through 9 m. Taking g=10 m/s², what increase in gravitational potential energy occurs?","options":["1530 J","153 J","170 J","765 J"],"answer":0,"explanation":"ΔPE=mgh.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-075","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A 16 kg trolley increases its speed from 18 m/s to 27 m/s. What impulse acts on it?","options":["144 N s","432 N s","288 N s","720 N s"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Impulse equals change in momentum: m(v−u).","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-076","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A resistor of 9 Ω carries a current of 16 A. What electrical power is dissipated?","options":["2304 W","144 W","25 W","0.5625 W"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Power P=I²R or VI.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-077","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A wave has frequency 19 Hz and wavelength 0.5 m. Calculate its speed.","options":["9.5 m/s","38 m/s","19.5 m/s","0.0263158 m/s"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Wave speed v=fλ.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-078","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A 5 kg object moves at 18 m/s in a circle of radius 16 m. What is the magnitude of its centripetal force?","options":["101.25 N","5.625 N","1440 N","25920 N"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Centripetal force is mv²/r.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-079","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A converging lens has focal length 0.22 m and forms a real image when an object is 1 m from it. What is the image distance?","options":["0.282 m","0.180 m","0.780 m","0.220 m"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Use the lens formula 1/f=1/u+1/v with consistent sign conventions for magnitudes in this real-object case.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-080","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"How much heat is needed to raise the temperature of 16 kg of water by 11 °C? Take c=4200 J kg⁻¹ °C⁻¹.","options":["739,200 J","67,200 J","46,200 J","73,920.0 J"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Heat supplied Q=mcΔT.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-081","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Light of wavelength 600 nm falls on a surface. Using h=6.63×10⁻³⁴ J s and c=3.0×10⁸ m/s, what is the energy of one photon?","options":["3.315e-19 J","1.326e-48 J","1.657e-19 J","1.193e-31 J"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Photon energy is E=hc/λ.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-082","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A car travels with initial speed 23 m/s and uniform acceleration 2 m/s² for 6 s. What distance does it cover?","options":["174 m","138 m","210 m","36 m"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Use s = ut + ½at².","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-083","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A 17 kg object is acted upon by a resultant force of 102 N. What acceleration does it acquire?","options":["6 m/s²","102 m/s²","17 m/s²","7 m/s²"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Newton’s second law gives a=F/m.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-084","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A load of mass 18 kg is lifted vertically through 10 m. Taking g=10 m/s², what increase in gravitational potential energy occurs?","options":["1800 J","180 J","900 J","Insufficient information to determine the answer"],"answer":0,"explanation":"ΔPE=mgh.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-085","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A 17 kg trolley increases its speed from 19 m/s to 24 m/s. What impulse acts on it?","options":["85 N s","408 N s","323 N s","731 N s"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Impulse equals change in momentum: m(v−u).","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-086","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A resistor of 10 Ω carries a current of 17 A. What electrical power is dissipated?","options":["2890 W","170 W","27 W","0.588235 W"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Power P=I²R o