:["108 N s","468 N s","360 N s","828 N s"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Impulse equals change in momentum: m(v−u).","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-097","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A resistor of 3 Ω carries a current of 18 A. What electrical power is dissipated?","options":["972 W","54 W","21 W","0.166667 W"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Power P=I²R or VI.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-098","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A wave has frequency 21 Hz and wavelength 0.2 m. Calculate its speed.","options":["4.2 m/s","105 m/s","21.2 m/s","0.00952381 m/s"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Wave speed v=fλ.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-099","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A 2 kg object moves at 20 m/s in a circle of radius 18 m. What is the magnitude of its centripetal force?","options":["44.4444 N","2.22222 N","720 N","14400 N"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Centripetal force is mv²/r.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-100","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A converging lens has focal length 0.1 m and forms a real image when an object is 1.1 m from it. What is the image distance?","options":["0.110 m","0.092 m","1.000 m","Insufficient information to determine the answer"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Use the lens formula 1/f=1/u+1/v with consistent sign conventions for magnitudes in this real-object case.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-101","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"How much heat is needed to raise the temperature of 18 kg of water by 5 °C? Take c=4200 J kg⁻¹ °C⁻¹.","options":["378,000 J","75,600 J","21,000 J","37,800.0 J"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Heat supplied Q=mcΔT.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-102","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Light of wavelength 640 nm falls on a surface. Using h=6.63×10⁻³⁴ J s and c=3.0×10⁸ m/s, what is the energy of one photon?","options":["3.108e-19 J","1.414e-48 J","1.554e-19 J","1.273e-31 J"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Photon energy is E=hc/λ.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-physics-roman-clean-017","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about a 162 kg body moving on a straight track are correct?\n\nI. If the resultant force is non-zero, its velocity changes.\nII. If the resultant force is zero, the body may still move at constant velocity.\nIII. For a given mass, doubling the resultant force doubles the acceleration.\nIV. Acceleration is measured in newtons.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; acceleration is measured in m/s², while the newton is a unit of force.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":true},{"id":"qb-physics-roman-clean-037","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about a circuit containing a 165 Ω resistor carrying 4 A are correct?\n\nI. The potential difference across the resistor is 660 V.\nII. The electrical power is 2640 W.\nIII. Ohm’s law gives V=IR for an ohmic resistor at constant physical conditions.\nIV. The resistance is found by multiplying voltage by current.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; resistance is R=V/I, not VI.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":true},{"id":"qb-physics-roman-clean-018","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about a wave of frequency 168 Hz and wavelength 1.89 m are correct?\n\nI. Its speed is fλ.\nII. Its period is 1/f.\nIII. If frequency increases while wavelength remains fixed, speed increases.\nIV. Frequency is measured in metres.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; frequency is measured in hertz.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":true},{"id":"qb-physics-roman-clean-038","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about a 167 kg object raised through 7 m are correct, taking g=10 m/s²?\n\nI. Its gravitational potential energy increases by mgh.\nII. The increase is 11690 J.\nIII. Raising it higher increases its gravitational potential energy.\nIV. Gravitational potential energy is measured in watts.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; energy is measured in joules, while the watt is a unit of power.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":true},{"id":"qb-physics-roman-clean-019","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about a 166 kg body moving on a straight track are correct?\n\nI. If the resultant force is non-zero, its velocity changes.\nII. If the resultant force is zero, the body may still move at constant velocity.\nIII. For a given mass, doubling the resultant force doubles the acceleration.\nIV. Acceleration is measured in newtons.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; acceleration is measured in m/s², while the newton is a unit of force.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":true},{"id":"qb-physics-roman-clean-039","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about a circuit containing a 169 Ω resistor carrying 3 A are correct?\n\nI. The potential difference across the resistor is 507 V.\nII. The electrical power is 1521 W.\nIII. Ohm’s law gives V=IR for an ohmic resistor at constant physical conditions.\nIV. The resistance is found by multiplying voltage by current.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; resistance is R=V/I, not VI.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":true},{"id":"qb-physics-roman-clean-020","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about a wave of frequency 172 Hz and wavelength 1.93 m are correct?\n\nI. Its speed is fλ.\nII. Its period is 1/f.\nIII. If frequency increases while wavelength remains fixed, speed increases.\nIV. Frequency is measured in metres.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; frequency is measured in hertz.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":true},{"id":"qb-physics-roman-clean-040","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about a 171 kg object raised through 4 m are correct, taking g=10 m/s²?\n\nI. Its gravitational potential energy increases by mgh.\nII. The increase is 6840 J.\nIII. Raising it higher increases its gravitational potential energy.\nIV. Gravitational potential energy is measured in watts.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; energy is measured in joules, while the watt is a unit of power.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":true},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-103","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"How much heat is needed to raise the temperature of 19 kg of water by 6 °C? Take c=4200 J kg⁻¹ °C⁻¹.","options":["478,800 J","79,800 J","25,200 J","47,880.0 J"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Heat supplied Q=mcΔT.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-104","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Light of wavelength 660 nm falls on a surface. Using h=6.63×10⁻³⁴ J s and c=3.0×10⁸ m/s, what is the energy of one photon?","options":["3.014e-19 J","1.459e-48 J","1.507e-19 J","1.313e-31 J"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Photon energy is E=hc/λ.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-105","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A car travels with initial speed 26 m/s and uniform acceleration 5 m/s² for 3 s. What distance does it cover?","options":["100.5 m","78 m","123 m","22.5 m"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Use s = ut + ½at².","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-107","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A 20 kg object is acted upon by a resultant force of 60 N. What acceleration does it acquire?","options":["3 m/s²","60 m/s²","20 m/s²","4 m/s²"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Newton’s second law gives a=F/m.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-108","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A load of mass 21 kg is lifted vertically through 4 m. Taking g=10 m/s², what increase in gravitational potential energy occurs?","options":["840 J","84 J","210 J","420 J"],"answer":0,"explanation":"ΔPE=mgh.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-109","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A 20 kg trolley increases its speed from 22 m/s to 30 m/s. What impulse acts on it?","options":["160 N s","600 N s","440 N s","1040 N s"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Impulse equals change in momentum: m(v−u).","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-110","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A resistor of 5 Ω carries a current of 20 A. What electrical power is dissipated?","options":["2000 W","100 W","25 W","0.25 W"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Power P=I²R or VI.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-111","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A wave has frequency 23 Hz and wavelength 0.3 m. Calculate its speed.","options":["6.9 m/s","76.6667 m/s","23.3 m/s","0.0130435 m/s"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Wave speed v=fλ.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-112","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A 4 kg object moves at 22 m/s in a circle of radius 20 m. What is the magnitude of its centripetal force?","options":["96.8 N","4.4 N","1760 N","38720 N"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Centripetal force is mv²/r.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-113","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A converging lens has focal length 0.14 m and forms a real image when an object is 1.2 m from it. What is the image distance?","options":["0.158 m","0.125 m","1.060 m","0.168 m"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Use the lens formula 1/f=1/u+1/v with consistent sign conventions for magnitudes in this real-object case.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-114","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"How much heat is needed to raise the temperature of 20 kg of water by 7 °C? Take c=4200 J kg⁻¹ °C⁻¹.","options":["588,000 J","84,000 J","29,400 J","58,800.0 J"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Heat supplied Q=mcΔT.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Physics","roman":false},{"id":"qb-phys-gen-115","type":"mcq","passageId"