2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Chemistry","roman":false},{"id":"qb-chemistry-gen-1061","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A compound contains 216 g carbon, 36 g hydrogen and 32 g oxygen. What is its empirical formula?","options":["C9H18O1","C10H18O1","C9H19O1","C9H18O2"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Convert each mass to moles, divide by the smallest mole value and reduce to the simplest whole-number ratio.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Chemistry","roman":false},{"id":"qb-chemistry-gen-1064","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"What is the oxidation number of chlorine in ClO⁻?","options":["+1","+3","+5","−1"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Assign the usual oxidation numbers to the other atoms and use the overall charge of the species to solve for chlorine.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Chemistry","roman":false},{"id":"qb-chemistry-gen-1067","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A current of 18 A flows for 180 s. Approximately how many moles of electrons pass through the circuit? Take F=96,500 C mol⁻¹.","options":["0.0336 mol","3240 mol","0.0672 mol","0.10000 mol"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Charge Q=It; moles of electrons=Q/F.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Chemistry","roman":false},{"id":"qb-chemistry-gen-1068","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"At 476 K, for the equilibrium CO + H₂O ⇌ CO₂ + H₂, which change would favour the products under the stated equilibrium conditions?","options":["removing a product","adding more product","adding a catalyst to shift equilibrium","removing a reactant"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Removing a product shifts equilibrium towards products to oppose the change.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Chemistry","roman":false},{"id":"qb-chemistry-roman-clean-017","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about an element with atomic number 170 are correct?\n\nI. Its neutral atom contains 170 electrons.\nII. Its proton number is 170.\nIII. A +1 ion of the element contains 169 electrons.\nIV. Its atomic number changes when it forms an ion.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; ion formation changes electron number, not atomic number.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Chemistry","roman":true},{"id":"qb-chemistry-roman-clean-037","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about 3.26 mol dm⁻³ of a strong monoprotic acid are correct?\n\nI. It ionises extensively in water.\nII. Its hydrogen-ion concentration is approximately 3.26 mol dm⁻³.\nIII. Its pH is determined from −log[H⁺].\nIV. Complete ionisation means the acid contains no hydrogen atoms.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; ionisation in water does not mean the acid molecule contains no hydrogen.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Chemistry","roman":true},{"id":"qb-chemistry-roman-clean-018","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about the electrolysis of an aqueous solution of potassium iodide using a current of 163 A are correct?\n\nI. Reduction occurs at the cathode.\nII. Oxidation occurs at the anode.\nIII. Cations migrate towards the cathode.\nIV. Electrons are the principal charge carriers throughout the electrolyte solution.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; ions carry charge through the electrolyte.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Chemistry","roman":true},{"id":"qb-chemistry-roman-clean-038","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about an alkane containing 169 carbon atoms are correct?\n\nI. Its general formula is CₙH₂ₙ₊₂.\nII. Its molecular formula is C169H340.\nIII. It is a saturated hydrocarbon.\nIV. It must contain a carbon–carbon triple bond.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; alkanes are saturated and do not contain triple bonds.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Chemistry","roman":true},{"id":"qb-chemistry-roman-clean-019","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about an element with atomic number 174 are correct?\n\nI. Its neutral atom contains 174 electrons.\nII. Its proton number is 174.\nIII. A +1 ion of the element contains 173 electrons.\nIV. Its atomic number changes when it forms an ion.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; ion formation changes electron number, not atomic number.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Chemistry","roman":true},{"id":"qb-chemistry-roman-clean-039","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about 3.34 mol dm⁻³ of a strong monoprotic acid are correct?\n\nI. It ionises extensively in water.\nII. Its hydrogen-ion concentration is approximately 3.34 mol dm⁻³.\nIII. Its pH is determined from −log[H⁺].\nIV. Complete ionisation means the acid contains no hydrogen atoms.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; ionisation in water does not mean the acid molecule contains no hydrogen.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Chemistry","roman":true},{"id":"qb-chemistry-roman-clean-020","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about the electrolysis of an aqueous solution of lead(II) bromide using a current of 167 A are correct?\n\nI. Reduction occurs at the cathode.\nII. Oxidation occurs at the anode.\nIII. Cations migrate towards the cathode.\nIV. Electrons are the principal charge carriers throughout the electrolyte solution.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; ions carry charge through the electrolyte.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Chemistry","roman":true},{"id":"qb-chemistry-roman-clean-040","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about an alkane containing 173 carbon atoms are correct?\n\nI. Its general formula is CₙH₂ₙ₊₂.\nII. Its molecular formula is C173H348.\nIII. It is a saturated hydrocarbon.\nIV. It must contain a carbon–carbon triple bond.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; alkanes are saturated and do not contain triple bonds.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Chemistry","roman":true},{"id":"qb-chemistry-gen-1070","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A current of 19 A flows for 240 s. Approximately how many moles of electrons pass through the circuit? Take F=96,500 C mol⁻¹.","options":["0.0473 mol","4560 mol","0.0945 mol","0.07917 mol"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Charge Q=It; moles of electrons=Q/F.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Chemistry","roman":false},{"id":"qb-chemistry-gen-1074","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"At 487 K, for the equilibrium N₂ + 3H₂ ⇌ 2NH₃, which change would favour the products under the stated equilibrium conditions?","options":["lowering the temperature","raising the temperature","adding a catalyst","removing nitrogen"],"answer":0,"explanation":"For an exothermic forward reaction, lowering temperature favours the product side.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Chemistry","roman":false},{"id":"qb-chemistry-gen-1077","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A sample of carbon dioxide has a mass of 30 g. If Mr(CO₂)=44, how many moles of CO₂ are present?","options":["0.682 mol","1320.0 mol","1.467 mol","30.000 mol"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Moles = mass/Mr.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Chemistry","roman":false},{"id":"qb-chemistry-gen-1078","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"What mass of NaOH (Mr=40) is required to prepare 0.46 dm³ of a 0.23 mol dm⁻³ solution?","options":["4.232 g","9.200 g","18.400 g","20.000 g"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Use n=CV and mass=nMr.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Chemistry","roman":false},{"id":"qb-chemistry-gen-1084","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A gas occupies 22 dm³ at 20 atm. What volume will it occupy at 3 atm at constant temperature?","options":["146.667 dm³","3.3 dm³","66 dm³","39 dm³"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Boyle’s law: P₁V₁=P₂V₂.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Chemistry","roman":false},{"id":"qb-chemistry-gen-1087","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which molecular formula represents the alkane containing 22 carbon atoms?","options":["C22H46","C22H44","C22H42","C23H46"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Alkanes have the general formula CₙH₂ₙ₊₂.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Chemistry","roman":false},{"id":"qb-chemistry-gen-1088","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"An ion has atomic number 24 and a charge of 1+. How many electrons does it contain?","options":["23","24","25","1"],"answer":0,"explanation":"A positive ion has lost electrons, so electrons=atomic number−charge.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Chemistry","roman":false},{"id":"qb-chemistry-gen-1094","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A strong monoprotic acid has concentration 0.019 mol dm⁻³. What is its approximate pH?","options":["1.72","2.72","12.28","0.72"],"answer":0,"explanation":"For a strong monoprotic acid, [H⁺]≈c and pH=−log[H⁺].","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Chemistry","roman":false},{"id":"qb-chemistry-gen-1097","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A compound contains 240 g carbon, 40 g hydrogen and 16 g oxygen. What is its empirical formula?","options":["C20H40O1","C21H40O1","C20H41O1","C20H40O2"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Convert each mass to moles, divide by the smallest mole value and reduce to the simplest whole-number ratio.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Chemistry","roman":false},{"id":"qb-chemistry-gen-1098","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"What is the oxidation number of phosphorus in PCl₅?","options":["+5","+3","−3","−1"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Assign the usual oxidation numbers to the other atoms and use the overall charge of the species to solve for phosphorus.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Chemistry","roman":false},{"id":"qb-chemistry-gen-1104","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A current of 20 A flows for 300 s. Approximately how many moles of electrons pass through the circuit? Take F=96,500 C mol⁻¹.","options":["0.0622 mol","6000 mol","0.1244 mol","0.06667 mol"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Charge Q=It; moles of electrons=Q/F.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Chemistry","roman":false},{"id":"qb-chemistry-gen-1107","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"At 498 K, for the equilibrium 2SO₂ + O₂ ⇌ 2SO₃, which change would favour the products under the stated equilibrium conditions?","options":["increasing the pressure","decreasing the pressure","adding an inert gas at constant volume","raising the temperature for an exothermic forward reaction"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The product side has fewer gas molecules, so increasing pressure favours products.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Chemistry","roman":false},{"id":"qb-chemistry-gen-1108","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A sample of carbon dioxide has a mass of 31 g. If Mr(CO₂)=44, how many moles of CO₂ are present?","options":["0.705 mol","1364.0 mol","1.419 mol","31.000 mol"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Moles = mass/Mr.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Chemistry","roman":false},{"id":"qb-chemistry-gen-1114","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"What mass of NaOH (Mr=40) is required to prepare 0.48 dm³ of a 0.24 mol dm⁻³ solution?","options":["4.608 g","9.600 g","19.200 g","20.000 g"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Use n=CV and mass=nMr.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Chemistry","roman":false},{"id":"qb-chemistry-gen-1117","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A gas occupies 23 dm³ at 21 atm. What volume will it occupy at 4 atm at constant temperature?","options":["120.75 dm³","4.38095 dm³","92 dm³","40 dm³"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Boyle’s law: P₁V₁=P₂V₂.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Chemistry","roman":false},{"id":"qb-chemistry-gen-1118","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which molecular formula represents the alkane containing 23 carbon atoms?","options":["C23H48","C23H46","C23H44","C24H48"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Alkanes have the general formula CₙH₂ₙ₊₂.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Chemistry","roman":false},{"id":"qb-chemistry-gen-1124","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"An ion has atomic number 25 and a charge of 2+. How many electrons does it contain?","options":["23","25","27","2"],"answer":0,"explanation":"A positive ion has lost electrons, so electrons=atomic number−charge.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Chemistry","roman":false},{"id":"qb-chemistry-gen-1127","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A strong monoprotic acid has concentration 0.02 mol dm⁻³. What is its approximate pH?","options":["1.70","2.70","12.30","0.70"],"answer":0,"explanation":"For a strong monoprotic acid, [H⁺]≈c and pH=−log[H⁺].","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Chemistry","roman":false},{"id":"qb-chemistry-gen-1128","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A compound contains 252 g carbon, 42 g hydrogen and 32 g oxygen. What is its empirical formula?","options":["C10H21O1","C11H21O1","C10H22O1","C10H21O2"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Convert each mass to moles, divide by the smallest mole value and reduce to the simplest whole-number ratio.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Chemistry","roman":false},{"id":"qb-chemistry-gen-1134","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"What is the oxidation number of carbon in CH₄?","options":["−4","+4","+2","−2"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Assign the usual oxidation numbers to the other atoms and use the overall charge of the species to solve for carbon.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Chemistry","roman":false},{"id":"qb-chemistry-gen-1137","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A current of 21 A flows for 360 s. Approximately how many moles of electrons pass through the circuit? Take F=96,500 C mol⁻¹.","options":["0.0783 mol","7560 mol","0.1567 mol","0.05833 mol"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Charge Q=It; moles of electrons=Q/F.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Chemistry","roman":false},{"id":"qb-chemistry-gen-1138","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"At 509 K, for the equilibrium H₂ + I₂ ⇌ 2HI, which change would favour the products under the stated equilibrium conditions?","options":["changing concentrations according to Le Chatelier’s principle","using a catalyst to change Kc","removing all reactants","stopping the reaction at equilibrium"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Changing concentrations can shift equilibrium according to Le Chatelier’s principle; a catalyst does not change equilibrium position.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Chemistry","roman":false},{"id":"qb-chemistry-gen-1144","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A sample of carbon dioxide has a mass of 32 g. If Mr(CO₂)=44, how many moles of CO₂ are present?","options":["0.727 mol","1408.0 mol","1.375 mol","32.000 mol"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Moles = mass/Mr.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Chemistry","roman":false},{"id":"qb-chemistry-gen-1147","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"What mass of NaOH (Mr=40) is required to prepare 0.5 dm³ of a 0.25 mol dm⁻³ solution?","options":["5.000 g","10.000 g","20.000 g","Insufficient information to determine the answer"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Use n=CV and mass=nMr.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Chemistry","roman":false},{"id":"qb-chemistry-gen-1148","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A gas occupies 24 dm³ at 22 atm. What volume will it occupy at 5 atm at constant temperature?","options":["105.6 dm³","5.45455 dm³","120 dm³","41 dm³"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Boyle’s law: P₁V₁=P₂V₂.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Chemistry","roman":false},{"id":"qb-chemistry-gen-1154","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which molecular formula represents the alkane containing 24 carbon atoms?","options":["C24H50","C24H48","C24H46","C25H50"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Alkanes have the general formula CₙH₂ₙ₊₂.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Chemistry","roman":false},{"id":"qb-chemistry-gen-1157","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"An ion has atomic number 26 and a charge of 3+. How many electrons does it contain?","options":["23","26","29","3"],"answer":0,"explanation":"A positive ion has lost electrons, so electrons=atomic number−charge.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Chemistry","roman":false},{"id":"qb-chemistry-gen-1158","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A strong monoprotic acid has concentration 0.021 mol dm⁻³. What is its approximate pH?","options":["1.68","2.68","12.32","0.68"],"answer":0,"explanation":"For a strong monoprotic acid, [H⁺]≈c and pH=−log[H⁺].","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Chemistry","roman":false},{"id":"qb-chemistry-gen-1164","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A compound contains 264 g carbon, 44 g hydrogen and 48 g oxygen. What is its empirical formula?","options":["C7H15O1","C8H15O1","C7H16O1","C7H15O2"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Convert each mass to moles, divide by the smallest mole value and reduce to the simplest whole-number ratio.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Chemistry","roman":false},{"id":"qb-chemistry-gen-1167","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"What is the oxidation number of nitrogen in N₂O?","options":["+1","+3","−1","−3"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Assign the usual oxidation numbers to the other atoms and use the overall charge of the species to solve for nitrogen.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Chemistry","roman":false},{"id":"qb-chemistry-gen-1168","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A current of 22 A flows for 120 s. Approximately how many moles of electrons pass through the circuit? Take F=96,500 C mol⁻¹.","options":["0.0274 mol","2640 mol","0.0547 mol","0.18333 mol"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Charge Q=It; moles of electrons=Q/F.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Chemistry","roman":false},{"id":"qb-chemistry-gen-1174","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"At 520 K, for the equilibrium CO + H₂O ⇌ CO₂ + H₂, which change would favour the products under the stated equilibrium conditions?","options":["removing a product","adding more product","adding a catalyst to shift equilibrium","removing a reactant"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Removing a product shifts equilibrium towards products to oppose the change.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Chemistry","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-roman-clean-001","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about the plasma membrane of a liver cell maintained at approximately 25 °C are correct?\n\nI. The membrane is selectively permeable.\nII. Phospholipids form the basic bilayer.\nIII. Some membrane proteins facilitate movement of substances.\nIV. Every substance crosses the membrane by simple diffusion.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; some substances require facilitated diffusion or active transport.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":true},{"id":"qb-biology-roman-clean-021","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about inheritance in a diploid organism with 3 chromosome pairs are correct?\n\nI. Alleles are alternative forms of a gene.\nII. Meiosis can generate new allele combinations.\nIII. DNA carries hereditary information.\nIV. Every mutation produces a harmful phenotype.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; mutations may be harmful, neutral or beneficial.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":true},{"id":"qb-biology-roman-clean-002","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about a population of 1400 organisms are correct?\n\nI. Births can increase population size.\nII. Deaths can reduce population size.\nIII. Immigration can increase population size.\nIV. Emigration always increases population size.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; emigration removes individuals from the population.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":true},{"id":"qb-biology-roman-clean-022","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about human regulation are correct when blood glucose is approximately 79 mg/dL?\n\nI. Insulin helps lower blood glucose concentration.\nII. ADH promotes water reabsorption in the kidney.\nIII. Negative feedback helps maintain internal stability.\nIV. Hormones act only on cells that have no receptors for them.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; hormones exert effects through appropriate receptors.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":true},{"id":"qb-biology-roman-clean-003","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about the plasma membrane of a guard cell maintained at approximately 29 °C are correct?\n\nI. The membrane is selectively permeable.\nII. Phospholipids form the basic bilayer.\nIII. Some membrane proteins facilitate movement of substances.\nIV. Every substance crosses the membrane by simple diffusion.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; some substances require facilitated diffusion or active transport.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":true},{"id":"qb-biology-roman-clean-023","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about inheritance in a diploid organism with 7 chromosome pairs are correct?\n\nI. Alleles are alternative forms of a gene.\nII. Meiosis can generate new allele combinations.\nIII. DNA carries hereditary information.\nIV. Every mutation produces a harmful phenotype.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; mutations may be harmful, neutral or beneficial.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":true},{"id":"qb-biology-roman-clean-004","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about a population of 1800 organisms are correct?\n\nI. Births can increase population size.\nII. Deaths can reduce population size.\nIII. Immigration can increase population size.\nIV. Emigration always increases population size.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; emigration removes individuals from the population.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":true},{"id":"qb-biology-roman-clean-024","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about human regulation are correct when blood glucose is approximately 91 mg/dL?\n\nI. Insulin helps lower blood glucose concentration.\nII. ADH promotes water reabsorption in the kidney.\nIII. Negative feedback helps maintain internal stability.\nIV. Hormones act only on cells that have no receptors for them.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; hormones exert effects through appropriate receptors.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":true},{"id":"qb-biology-01","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"In a large randomly mating population, the frequency of an autosomal recessive allele is 0.06. Assuming Hardy–Weinberg conditions, what is the expected frequency of heterozygotes?","options":["0.11","0.00","0.88","1.00"],"answer":0,"explanation":"With q as the recessive-allele frequency, p=1−q and heterozygotes occur at 2pq.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-02","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"If a producer stores 10,500 kJ of chemical energy and approximately 10% is transferred to the next trophic level, how much energy is available there?","options":["1,050 kJ","105 kJ","5,250 kJ","9,500 kJ"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Using the ecological efficiency approximation, 10% of the energy is transferred to the next trophic level.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-03","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"In a cross between two heterozygous plants with alleles P and p, where P is dominant for purple and p is recessive for white, what proportion of offspring is expected to show white?","options":["25%","50%","75%","100%"],"answer":0,"explanation":"A heterozygous × heterozygous cross gives a 1:2:1 genotype ratio and therefore 25% recessive phenotype.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-04","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A plant transpires at an average rate of 4 cm³ of water per hour for 7 hours. How much water is lost in that period?","options":["28 cm³","11 cm³","0.57 cm³","32 cm³"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Total water loss = rate × time.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-05","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"In a healthy adult, alveolar oxygen partial pressure is 89 mmHg while venous blood oxygen partial pressure is 37 mmHg. Which gas will diffuse from the alveolus into the blood?","options":["Oxygen","Carbon dioxide","Nitrogen","Water vapour"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Oxygen moves down its partial-pressure gradient from alveolar air into venous blood.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-06","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which process most directly contributes to genetic variation by metaphase I of meiosis?","options":["independent assortment","binary fission","mitosis","cytokinesis"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Independent assortment contributes to genetic variation in the stated context.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-07","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A population contains 2200 organisms. In one year there are 134 births, 78 deaths, 36 immigrants and 24 emigrants. What is the net increase?","options":["68","56","12","78"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Net population change = births − deaths + immigration − emigration.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-08","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which hormone is most directly associated with the following physiological effect: raise blood glucose during fasting?","options":["glucagon","insulin","thyroxine","ADH"],"answer":0,"explanation":"glucagon has the stated physiological role.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-09","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which structure is best adapted to provide a large surface area for gas exchange?","options":["alveoli — provide a large surface area for gas exchange","phloem sieve tubes — translocate organic solutes","lysosomes — digest cellular materials","cartilage — reduce friction at joints"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Alveoli is specialised for the stated function.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-10","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which option correctly matches phloem with its principal role?","options":["phloem — organic solutes","neurones — nerve impulses","guard cells — stomatal regulation","pancreas — digestive enzymes and hormones"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The selected structure is correctly matched with its principal role.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-11","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"In a large randomly mating population, the frequency of an autosomal recessive allele is 0.07. Assuming Hardy–Weinberg conditions, what is the expected frequency of heterozygotes?","options":["0.13","0.00","0.86","1.00"],"answer":0,"explanation":"With q as the recessive-allele frequency, p=1−q and heterozygotes occur at 2pq.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-12","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"If a producer stores 11,000 kJ of chemical energy and approximately 10% is transferred to the next trophic level, how much energy is available there?","options":["1,100 kJ","110 kJ","5,500 kJ","10,000 kJ"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Using the ecological efficiency approximation, 10% of the energy is transferred to the next trophic level.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-13","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"In a cross between two heterozygous plants with alleles R and r, where R is dominant for round and r is recessive for wrinkled, what proportion of offspring is expected to show wrinkled?","options":["25%","50%","75%","100%"],"answer":0,"explanation":"A heterozygous × heterozygous cross gives a 1:2:1 genotype ratio and therefore 25% recessive phenotype.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-14","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A plant transpires at an average rate of 5 cm³ of water per hour for 8 hours. How much water is lost in that period?","options":["40 cm³","13 cm³","0.62 cm³","45 cm³"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Total water loss = rate × time.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-15","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"In a healthy adult, alveolar oxygen partial pressure is 91 mmHg while venous blood oxygen partial pressure is 38 mmHg. Which gas will diffuse from the alveolus into the blood?","options":["Oxygen","Carbon dioxide","Nitrogen","Water vapour"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Oxygen moves down its partial-pressure gradient from alveolar air into venous blood.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-16","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which process most directly contributes to genetic variation by fertilisation?","options":["random fertilisation","binary fission","mitosis","cytokinesis"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Random fertilisation contributes to genetic variation in the stated context.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-17","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A population contains 2300 organisms. In one year there are 141 births, 82 deaths, 39 immigrants and 26 emigrants. What is the net increase?","options":["72","59","13","82"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Net population change = births − deaths + immigration − emigration.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-18","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which hormone is most directly associated with the following physiological effect: increase water reabsorption by the kidneys?","options":["ADH","insulin","thyroxine","cortisol"],"answer":0,"explanation":"ADH has the stated physiological role.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-19","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which structure is best adapted to increase the surface area for mineral and water absorption?","options":["root hairs — increase the surface area for mineral and water absorption","red blood cells — transport oxygen efficiently","guard cells — control stomatal opening","tendons — attach muscles to bones"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Root hairs is specialised for the stated function.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-20","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which option correctly matches red blood cells with its principal role?","options":["red blood cells — oxygen","ciliated epithelial cells — movement of mucus","sperm cells — fertilisation of the ovum","trachea — air passage"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The selected structure is correctly matched with its principal role.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-21","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"In a large randomly mating population, the frequency of an autosomal recessive allele is 0.08. Assuming Hardy–Weinberg conditions, what is the expected frequency of heterozygotes?","options":["0.15","0.01","0.85","1.00"],"answer":0,"explanation":"With q as the recessive-allele frequency, p=1−q and heterozygotes occur at 2pq.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-22","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"If a producer stores 11,500 kJ of chemical energy and approximately 10% is transferred to the next trophic level, how much energy is available there?","options":["1,150 kJ","115 kJ","5,750 kJ","10,500 kJ"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Using the ecological efficiency approximation, 10% of the energy is transferred to the next trophic level.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-23","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"In a cross between two heterozygous plants with alleles Y and y, where Y is dominant for yellow and y is recessive for green, what proportion of offspring is expected to show green?","options":["25%","50%","75%","100%"],"answer":0,"explanation":"A heterozygous × heterozygous cross gives a 1:2:1 genotype ratio and therefore 25% recessive phenotype.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-24","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A plant transpires at an average rate of 6 cm³ of water per hour for 9 hours. How much water is lost in that period?","options":["54 cm³","15 cm³","0.67 cm³","60 cm³"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Total water loss = rate × time.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-25","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"In a healthy adult, alveolar oxygen partial pressure is 93 mmHg while venous blood oxygen partial pressure is 39 mmHg. Which gas will diffuse from the alveolus into the blood?","options":["Oxygen","Carbon dioxide","Nitrogen","Water vapour"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Oxygen moves down its partial-pressure gradient from alveolar air into venous blood.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-26","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which process most directly contributes to genetic variation by DNA sequence?","options":["mutation","binary fission","mitosis","cytokinesis"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Mutation contributes to genetic variation in the stated context.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-27","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A population contains 2400 organisms. In one year there are 148 births, 86 deaths, 42 immigrants and 28 emigrants. What is the net increase?","options":["76","62","14","86"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Net population change = births − deaths + immigration − emigration.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-28","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which hormone is most directly associated with the following physiological effect: increase basal metabolic activity?","options":["thyroxine","insulin","adrenaline","ADH"],"answer":0,"explanation":"thyroxine has the stated physiological role.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-29","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which structure is best adapted to filter blood and form urine?","options":["nephrons — filter blood and form urine","mitochondria — carry out aerobic respiration","myelin sheath — speed up impulse conduction","ligaments — connect bone to bone"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Nephrons is specialised for the stated function.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-30","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which option correctly matches white blood cells with its principal role?","options":["white blood cells — immune defence","muscle fibres — contraction","ovaries — ova and female sex hormones","alveoli — gas exchange"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The selected structure is correctly matched with its principal role.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-bio-gen-001","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"In a large randomly mating population, the frequency of an autosomal recessive allele is 0.09. Assuming Hardy–Weinberg conditions, what is the expected frequency of heterozygotes?","options":["0.16","0.01","0.83","1.00"],"answer":0,"explanation":"With q as the recessive-allele frequency, p=1−q and heterozygotes occur at 2pq.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-bio-gen-002","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"If a producer stores 12,000 kJ of chemical energy and approximately 10% is transferred to the next trophic level, how much energy is available there?","options":["1,200 kJ","120 kJ","6,000 kJ","11,000 kJ"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Using the ecological efficiency approximation, 10% of the energy is transferred to the next trophic level.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-roman-clean-005","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about the plasma membrane of a liver cell maintained at approximately 65 °C are correct?\n\nI. The membrane is selectively permeable.\nII. Phospholipids form the basic bilayer.\nIII. Some membrane proteins facilitate movement of substances.\nIV. Every substance crosses the membrane by simple diffusion.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; some substances require facilitated diffusion or active transport.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":true},{"id":"qb-biology-roman-clean-025","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about inheritance in a diploid organism with 43 chromosome pairs are correct?\n\nI. Alleles are alternative forms of a gene.\nII. Meiosis can generate new allele combinations.\nIII. DNA carries hereditary information.\nIV. Every mutation produces a harmful phenotype.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; mutations may be harmful, neutral or beneficial.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":true},{"id":"qb-biology-roman-clean-006","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about a population of 5400 organisms are correct?\n\nI. Births can increase population size.\nII. Deaths can reduce population size.\nIII. Immigration can increase population size.\nIV. Emigration always increases population size.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; emigration removes individuals from the population.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":true},{"id":"qb-biology-roman-clean-026","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about human regulation are correct when blood glucose is approximately 199 mg/dL?\n\nI. Insulin helps lower blood glucose concentration.\nII. ADH promotes water reabsorption in the kidney.\nIII. Negative feedback helps maintain internal stability.\nIV. Hormones act only on cells that have no receptors for them.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; hormones exert effects through appropriate receptors.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":true},{"id":"qb-biology-roman-clean-007","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about the plasma membrane of a guard cell maintained at approximately 69 °C are correct?\n\nI. The membrane is selectively permeable.\nII. Phospholipids form the basic bilayer.\nIII. Some membrane proteins facilitate movement of substances.\nIV. Every substance crosses the membrane by simple diffusion.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; some substances require facilitated diffusion or active transport.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":true},{"id":"qb-biology-roman-clean-027","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about inheritance in a diploid organism with 47 chromosome pairs are correct?\n\nI. Alleles are alternative forms of a gene.\nII. Meiosis can generate new allele combinations.\nIII. DNA carries hereditary information.\nIV. Every mutation produces a harmful phenotype.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; mutations may be harmful, neutral or beneficial.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":true},{"id":"qb-biology-roman-clean-008","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about a population of 5800 organisms are correct?\n\nI. Births can increase population size.\nII. Deaths can reduce population size.\nIII. Immigration can increase population size.\nIV. Emigration always increases population size.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; emigration removes individuals from the population.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":true},{"id":"qb-biology-roman-clean-028","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about human regulation are correct when blood glucose is approximately 211 mg/dL?\n\nI. Insulin helps lower blood glucose concentration.\nII. ADH promotes water reabsorption in the kidney.\nIII. Negative feedback helps maintain internal stability.\nIV. Hormones act only on cells that have no receptors for them.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; hormones exert effects through appropriate receptors.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":true},{"id":"qb-bio-gen-003","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"In a large randomly mating population, the frequency of an autosomal recessive allele is 0.10. Assuming Hardy–Weinberg conditions, what is the expected frequency of heterozygotes?","options":["0.18","0.01","0.81","1.00"],"answer":0,"explanation":"With q as the recessive-allele frequency, p=1−q and heterozygotes occur at 2pq.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-bio-gen-004","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"If a producer stores 12,500 kJ of chemical energy and approximately 10% is transferred to the next trophic level, how much energy is available there?","options":["1,250 kJ","125 kJ","6,250 kJ","11,500 kJ"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Using the ecological efficiency approximation, 10% of the energy is transferred to the next trophic level.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-bio-gen-005","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"In a cross between two heterozygous plants with alleles H and h, where H is dominant for hard and h is recessive for soft, what proportion of offspring is expected to show soft?","options":["25%","50%","75%","100%"],"answer":0,"explanation":"A heterozygous × heterozygous cross gives a 1:2:1 genotype ratio and therefore 25% recessive phenotype.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-bio-gen-006","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A plant transpires at an average rate of 3 cm³ of water per hour for 11 hours. How much water is lost in that period?","options":["33 cm³","14 cm³","0.27 cm³","36 cm³"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Total water loss = rate × time.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-bio-gen-007","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"In a healthy adult, alveolar oxygen partial pressure is 97 mmHg while venous blood oxygen partial pressure is 35 mmHg. Which gas will diffuse from the alveolus into the blood?","options":["Oxygen","Carbon dioxide","Nitrogen","Water vapour"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Oxygen moves down its partial-pressure gradient from alveolar air into venous blood.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-bio-gen-008","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which process most directly contributes to genetic variation by homologous chromosomes?","options":["recombination","binary fission","mitosis","cytokinesis"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Recombination contributes to genetic variation in the stated context.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-bio-gen-009","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A population contains 2600 organisms. In one year there are 162 births, 94 deaths, 48 immigrants and 32 emigrants. What is the net increase?","options":["84","68","16","94"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Net population change = births − deaths + immigration − emigration.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-bio-gen-010","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which hormone is most directly associated with the following physiological effect: promote female secondary sexual characteristics?","options":["oestrogen","insulin","thyroxine","ADH"],"answer":0,"explanation":"oestrogen has the stated physiological role.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-bio-gen-016","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which structure is best adapted to conduct water and mineral salts?","options":["xylem vessels — conduct water and mineral salts","chloroplasts — carry out photosynthesis","cartilage — reduce friction at joints","microvilli — increase absorptive surface area"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Xylem vessels is specialised for the stated function.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-bio-gen-026","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which option correctly matches neurones with its principal role?","options":["neurones — nerve impulses","root hairs — water absorption","kidneys — excretion and osmoregulation","xylem — water and mineral salts"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The selected structure is correctly matched with its principal role.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-bio-gen-036","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"In a large randomly mating population, the frequency of an autosomal recessive allele is 0.11. Assuming Hardy–Weinberg conditions, what is the expected frequency of heterozygotes?","options":["0.20","0.01","0.79","1.00"],"answer":0,"explanation":"With q as the recessive-allele frequency, p=1−q and heterozygotes occur at 2pq.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-bio-gen-046","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"If a producer stores 13,000 kJ of chemical energy and approximately 10% is transferred to the next trophic level, how much energy is available there?","options":["1,300 kJ","130 kJ","6,500 kJ","12,000 kJ"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Using the ecological efficiency approximation, 10% of the energy is transferred to the next trophic level.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-bio-gen-056","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"In a cross between two heterozygous plants with alleles S and s, where S is dominant for smooth and s is recessive for rough, what proportion of offspring is expected to show rough?","options":["25%","50%","75%","100%"],"answer":0,"explanation":"A heterozygous × heterozygous cross gives a 1:2:1 genotype ratio and therefore 25% recessive phenotype.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-bio-gen-076","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A plant transpires at an average rate of 4 cm³ of water per hour for 12 hours. How much water is lost in that period?","options":["48 cm³","16 cm³","0.33 cm³","52 cm³"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Total water loss = rate × time.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-bio-gen-086","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"In a healthy adult, alveolar oxygen partial pressure is 99 mmHg while venous blood oxygen partial pressure is 36 mmHg. Which gas will diffuse from the alveolus into the blood?","options":["Oxygen","Carbon dioxide","Nitrogen","Water vapour"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Oxygen moves down its partial-pressure gradient from alveolar air into venous blood.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-bio-gen-096","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which process most directly contributes to genetic variation by a nucleotide sequence?","options":["gene mutation","binary fission","mitosis","cytokinesis"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Gene mutation contributes to genetic variation in the stated context.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-bio-gen-106","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A population contains 2700 organisms. In one year there are 169 births, 98 deaths, 51 immigrants and 34 emigrants. What is the net increase?","options":["88","71","17","98"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Net population change = births − deaths + immigration − emigration.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1000","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which hormone is most directly associated with the following physiological effect: maintain the uterine lining during pregnancy?","options":["progesterone","insulin","thyroxine","ADH"],"answer":0,"explanation":"progesterone has the stated physiological role.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1001","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which structure is best adapted to translocate organic solutes?","options":["phloem sieve tubes — translocate organic solutes","lysosomes — digest cellular materials","tendons — attach muscles to bones","villi — increase absorptive surface area in the small intestine"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Phloem sieve tubes is specialised for the stated function.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1002","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which option correctly matches ciliated epithelial cells with its principal role?","options":["ciliated epithelial cells — movement of mucus","guard cells — stomatal regulation","liver — detoxification and bile production","phloem — organic solutes"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The selected structure is correctly matched with its principal role.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1003","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"In a large randomly mating population, the frequency of an autosomal recessive allele is 0.12. Assuming Hardy–Weinberg conditions, what is the expected frequency of heterozygotes?","options":["0.21","0.01","0.77","1.00"],"answer":0,"explanation":"With q as the recessive-allele frequency, p=1−q and heterozygotes occur at 2pq.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1004","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"If a producer stores 13,500 kJ of chemical energy and approximately 10% is transferred to the next trophic level, how much energy is available there?","options":["1,350 kJ","135 kJ","6,750 kJ","12,500 kJ"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Using the ecological efficiency approximation, 10% of the energy is transferred to the next trophic level.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1005","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"In a cross between two heterozygous plants with alleles A and a, where A is dominant for long and a is recessive for short, what proportion of offspring is expected to show short?","options":["25%","50%","75%","100%"],"answer":0,"explanation":"A heterozygous × heterozygous cross gives a 1:2:1 genotype ratio and therefore 25% recessive phenotype.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1006","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A plant transpires at an average rate of 5 cm³ of water per hour for 5 hours. How much water is lost in that period?","options":["25 cm³","10 cm³","1.00 cm³","30 cm³"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Total water loss = rate × time.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1007","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"In a healthy adult, alveolar oxygen partial pressure is 101 mmHg while venous blood oxygen partial pressure is 37 mmHg. Which gas will diffuse from the alveolus into the blood?","options":["Oxygen","Carbon dioxide","Nitrogen","Water vapour"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Oxygen moves down its partial-pressure gradient from alveolar air into venous blood.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1008","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which process most directly contributes to genetic variation by the orientation of homologous pairs?","options":["independent assortment","binary fission","mitosis","cytokinesis"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Independent assortment contributes to genetic variation in the stated context.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1009","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A population contains 2800 organisms. In one year there are 176 births, 102 deaths, 54 immigrants and 36 emigrants. What is the net increase?","options":["92","74","18","102"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Net population change = births − deaths + immigration − emigration.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1010","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which hormone is most directly associated with the following physiological effect: stimulate follicle development?","options":["FSH","insulin","thyroxine","ADH"],"answer":0,"explanation":"FSH has the stated physiological role.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1011","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which structure is best adapted to transport oxygen efficiently?","options":["red blood cells — transport oxygen efficiently","guard cells — control stomatal opening","ligaments — connect bone to bone","alveoli — provide a large surface area for gas exchange"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Red blood cells is specialised for the stated function.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1012","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which option correctly matches muscle fibres with its principal role?","options":["muscle fibres — contraction","sperm cells — fertilisation of the ovum","pancreas — digestive enzymes and hormones","red blood cells — oxygen"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The selected structure is correctly matched with its principal role.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1013","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"In a large randomly mating population, the frequency of an autosomal recessive allele is 0.13. Assuming Hardy–Weinberg conditions, what is the expected frequency of heterozygotes?","options":["0.23","0.02","0.76","1.00"],"answer":0,"explanation":"With q as the recessive-allele frequency, p=1−q and heterozygotes occur at 2pq.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1015","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"If a producer stores 14,000 kJ of chemical energy and approximately 10% is transferred to the next trophic level, how much energy is available there?","options":["1,400 kJ","140 kJ","7,000 kJ","13,000 kJ"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Using the ecological efficiency approximation, 10% of the energy is transferred to the next trophic level.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-roman-clean-009","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about the plasma membrane of a liver cell maintained at approximately 105 °C are correct?\n\nI. The membrane is selectively permeable.\nII. Phospholipids form the basic bilayer.\nIII. Some membrane proteins facilitate movement of substances.\nIV. Every substance crosses the membrane by simple diffusion.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; some substances require facilitated diffusion or active transport.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":true},{"id":"qb-biology-roman-clean-029","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about inheritance in a diploid organism with 83 chromosome pairs are correct?\n\nI. Alleles are alternative forms of a gene.\nII. Meiosis can generate new allele combinations.\nIII. DNA carries hereditary information.\nIV. Every mutation produces a harmful phenotype.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; mutations may be harmful, neutral or beneficial.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":true},{"id":"qb-biology-roman-clean-010","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about a population of 9400 organisms are correct?\n\nI. Births can increase population size.\nII. Deaths can reduce population size.\nIII. Immigration can increase population size.\nIV. Emigration always increases population size.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; emigration removes individuals from the population.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":true},{"id":"qb-biology-roman-clean-030","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about human regulation are correct when blood glucose is approximately 319 mg/dL?\n\nI. Insulin helps lower blood glucose concentration.\nII. ADH promotes water reabsorption in the kidney.\nIII. Negative feedback helps maintain internal stability.\nIV. Hormones act only on cells that have no receptors for them.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; hormones exert effects through appropriate receptors.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":true},{"id":"qb-biology-roman-clean-011","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about the plasma membrane of a guard cell maintained at approximately 109 °C are correct?\n\nI. The membrane is selectively permeable.\nII. Phospholipids form the basic bilayer.\nIII. Some membrane proteins facilitate movement of substances.\nIV. Every substance crosses the membrane by simple diffusion.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; some substances require facilitated diffusion or active transport.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":true},{"id":"qb-biology-roman-clean-031","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about inheritance in a diploid organism with 87 chromosome pairs are correct?\n\nI. Alleles are alternative forms of a gene.\nII. Meiosis can generate new allele combinations.\nIII. DNA carries hereditary information.\nIV. Every mutation produces a harmful phenotype.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; mutations may be harmful, neutral or beneficial.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":true},{"id":"qb-biology-roman-clean-012","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about a population of 9800 organisms are correct?\n\nI. Births can increase population size.\nII. Deaths can reduce population size.\nIII. Immigration can increase population size.\nIV. Emigration always increases population size.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; emigration removes individuals from the population.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":true},{"id":"qb-biology-roman-clean-032","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about human regulation are correct when blood glucose is approximately 331 mg/dL?\n\nI. Insulin helps lower blood glucose concentration.\nII. ADH promotes water reabsorption in the kidney.\nIII. Negative feedback helps maintain internal stability.\nIV. Hormones act only on cells that have no receptors for them.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; hormones exert effects through appropriate receptors.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":true},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1016","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"In a large randomly mating population, the frequency of an autosomal recessive allele is 0.14. Assuming Hardy–Weinberg conditions, what is the expected frequency of heterozygotes?","options":["0.24","0.02","0.74","1.00"],"answer":0,"explanation":"With q as the recessive-allele frequency, p=1−q and heterozygotes occur at 2pq.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1017","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"If a producer stores 14,500 kJ of chemical energy and approximately 10% is transferred to the next trophic level, how much energy is available there?","options":["1,450 kJ","145 kJ","7,250 kJ","13,500 kJ"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Using the ecological efficiency approximation, 10% of the energy is transferred to the next trophic level.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1018","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"In a cross between two heterozygous plants with alleles D and d, where D is dominant for dark and d is recessive for light, what proportion of offspring is expected to show light?","options":["25%","50%","75%","100%"],"answer":0,"explanation":"A heterozygous × heterozygous cross gives a 1:2:1 genotype ratio and therefore 25% recessive phenotype.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1019","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A plant transpires at an average rate of 2 cm³ of water per hour for 7 hours. How much water is lost in that period?","options":["14 cm³","9 cm³","0.29 cm³","16 cm³"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Total water loss = rate × time.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1020","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"In a healthy adult, alveolar oxygen partial pressure is 105 mmHg while venous blood oxygen partial pressure is 39 mmHg. Which gas will diffuse from the alveolus into the blood?","options":["Oxygen","Carbon dioxide","Nitrogen","Water vapour"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Oxygen moves down its partial-pressure gradient from alveolar air into venous blood.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1022","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which process most directly contributes to genetic variation by the union of different gametes?","options":["random fertilisation","binary fission","mitosis","cytokinesis"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Random fertilisation contributes to genetic variation in the stated context.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1023","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A population contains 3000 organisms. In one year there are 190 births, 110 deaths, 60 immigrants and 40 emigrants. What is the net increase?","options":["100","80","20","110"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Net population change = births − deaths + immigration − emigration.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1025","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which hormone is most directly associated with the following physiological effect: promote body growth?","options":["growth hormone","insulin","thyroxine","ADH"],"answer":0,"explanation":"growth hormone has the stated physiological role.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1026","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which structure is best adapted to synthesise proteins?","options":["ribosomes — synthesise proteins","synapses — permit communication between neurones","microvilli — increase absorptive surface area","nephrons — filter blood and form urine"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Ribosomes is specialised for the stated function.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1029","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which option correctly matches root hairs with its principal role?","options":["root hairs — water absorption","testes — sperm and testosterone","alveoli — gas exchange","platelets — blood clotting"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The selected structure is correctly matched with its principal role.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1030","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"In a large randomly mating population, the frequency of an autosomal recessive allele is 0.15. Assuming Hardy–Weinberg conditions, what is the expected frequency of heterozygotes?","options":["0.26","0.02","0.72","1.00"],"answer":0,"explanation":"With q as the recessive-allele frequency, p=1−q and heterozygotes occur at 2pq.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1031","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"If a producer stores 15,000 kJ of chemical energy and approximately 10% is transferred to the next trophic level, how much energy is available there?","options":["1,500 kJ","150 kJ","7,500 kJ","14,000 kJ"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Using the ecological efficiency approximation, 10% of the energy is transferred to the next trophic level.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1032","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"In a cross between two heterozygous plants with alleles E and e, where E is dominant for early and e is recessive for late, what proportion of offspring is expected to show late?","options":["25%","50%","75%","100%"],"answer":0,"explanation":"A heterozygous × heterozygous cross gives a 1:2:1 genotype ratio and therefore 25% recessive phenotype.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1033","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A plant transpires at an average rate of 3 cm³ of water per hour for 8 hours. How much water is lost in that period?","options":["24 cm³","11 cm³","0.38 cm³","27 cm³"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Total water loss = rate × time.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1034","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"In a healthy adult, alveolar oxygen partial pressure is 107 mmHg while venous blood oxygen partial pressure is 40 mmHg. Which gas will diffuse from the alveolus into the blood?","options":["Oxygen","Carbon dioxide","Nitrogen","Water vapour"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Oxygen moves down its partial-pressure gradient from alveolar air into venous blood.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1036","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which process most directly contributes to genetic variation by a change in genetic material?","options":["mutation","binary fission","mitosis","cytokinesis"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Mutation contributes to genetic variation in the stated context.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1037","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A population contains 3100 organisms. In one year there are 197 births, 114 deaths, 63 immigrants and 42 emigrants. What is the net increase?","options":["104","83","21","114"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Net population change = births − deaths + immigration − emigration.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1039","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which hormone is most directly associated with the following physiological effect: raise blood calcium concentration?","options":["parathyroid hormone","insulin","thyroxine","ADH"],"answer":0,"explanation":"parathyroid hormone has the stated physiological role.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1040","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which structure is best adapted to carry out photosynthesis?","options":["chloroplasts — carry out photosynthesis","cartilage — reduce friction at joints","villi — increase absorptive surface area in the small intestine","stomata — regulate gaseous exchange and water loss"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Chloroplasts is specialised for the stated function.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1043","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which option correctly matches guard cells with its principal role?","options":["guard cells — stomatal regulation","kidneys — excretion and osmoregulation","stomata — gaseous exchange","neurones — nerve impulses"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The selected structure is correctly matched with its principal role.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1044","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"In a large randomly mating population, the frequency of an autosomal recessive allele is 0.16. Assuming Hardy–Weinberg conditions, what is the expected frequency of heterozygotes?","options":["0.27","0.03","0.71","1.00"],"answer":0,"explanation":"With q as the recessive-allele frequency, p=1−q and heterozygotes occur at 2pq.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1045","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"If a producer stores 15,500 kJ of chemical energy and approximately 10% is transferred to the next trophic level, how much energy is available there?","options":["1,550 kJ","155 kJ","7,750 kJ","14,500 kJ"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Using the ecological efficiency approximation, 10% of the energy is transferred to the next trophic level.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1046","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"In a cross between two heterozygous plants with alleles F and f, where F is dominant for full and f is recessive for small, what proportion of offspring is expected to show small?","options":["25%","50%","75%","100%"],"answer":0,"explanation":"A heterozygous × heterozygous cross gives a 1:2:1 genotype ratio and therefore 25% recessive phenotype.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1047","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A plant transpires at an average rate of 4 cm³ of water per hour for 9 hours. How much water is lost in that period?","options":["36 cm³","13 cm³","0.44 cm³","40 cm³"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Total water loss = rate × time.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1048","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"In a healthy adult, alveolar oxygen partial pressure is 109 mmHg while venous blood oxygen partial pressure is 35 mmHg. Which gas will diffuse from the alveolus into the blood?","options":["Oxygen","Carbon dioxide","Nitrogen","Water vapour"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Oxygen moves down its partial-pressure gradient from alveolar air into venous blood.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1050","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which process most directly contributes to genetic variation by new allele combinations?","options":["recombination","binary fission","mitosis","cytokinesis"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Recombination contributes to genetic variation in the stated context.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1051","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A population contains 3200 organisms. In one year there are 204 births, 118 deaths, 66 immigrants and 44 emigrants. What is the net increase?","options":["108","86","22","118"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Net population change = births − deaths + immigration − emigration.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1053","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which hormone is most directly associated with the following physiological effect: lower blood calcium concentration?","options":["calcitonin","insulin","thyroxine","ADH"],"answer":0,"explanation":"calcitonin has the stated physiological role.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1054","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which structure is best adapted to digest cellular materials?","options":["lysosomes — digest cellular materials","tendons — attach muscles to bones","alveoli — provide a large surface area for gas exchange","xylem vessels — conduct water and mineral salts"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Lysosomes is specialised for the stated function.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1057","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which option correctly matches sperm cells with its principal role?","options":["sperm cells — fertilisation of the ovum","liver — detoxification and bile production","xylem — water and mineral salts","ciliated epithelial cells — movement of mucus"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The selected structure is correctly matched with its principal role.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1058","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"In a large randomly mating population, the frequency of an autosomal recessive allele is 0.17. Assuming Hardy–Weinberg conditions, what is the expected frequency of heterozygotes?","options":["0.28","0.03","0.69","1.00"],"answer":0,"explanation":"With q as the recessive-allele frequency, p=1−q and heterozygotes occur at 2pq.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1059","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"If a producer stores 16,000 kJ of chemical energy and approximately 10% is transferred to the next trophic level, how much energy is available there?","options":["1,600 kJ","160 kJ","8,000 kJ","15,000 kJ"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Using the ecological efficiency approximation, 10% of the energy is transferred to the next trophic level.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-roman-clean-013","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about the plasma membrane of a liver cell maintained at approximately 145 °C are correct?\n\nI. The membrane is selectively permeable.\nII. Phospholipids form the basic bilayer.\nIII. Some membrane proteins facilitate movement of substances.\nIV. Every substance crosses the membrane by simple diffusion.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; some substances require facilitated diffusion or active transport.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":true},{"id":"qb-biology-roman-clean-033","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about inheritance in a diploid organism with 123 chromosome pairs are correct?\n\nI. Alleles are alternative forms of a gene.\nII. Meiosis can generate new allele combinations.\nIII. DNA carries hereditary information.\nIV. Every mutation produces a harmful phenotype.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; mutations may be harmful, neutral or beneficial.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":true},{"id":"qb-biology-roman-clean-014","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about a population of 13400 organisms are correct?\n\nI. Births can increase population size.\nII. Deaths can reduce population size.\nIII. Immigration can increase population size.\nIV. Emigration always increases population size.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; emigration removes individuals from the population.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":true},{"id":"qb-biology-roman-clean-034","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about human regulation are correct when blood glucose is approximately 439 mg/dL?\n\nI. Insulin helps lower blood glucose concentration.\nII. ADH promotes water reabsorption in the kidney.\nIII. Negative feedback helps maintain internal stability.\nIV. Hormones act only on cells that have no receptors for them.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","