ce population size.\nIII. Immigration can increase population size.\nIV. Emigration always increases population size.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; emigration removes individuals from the population.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":true},{"id":"qb-biology-roman-clean-036","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which statements about human regulation are correct when blood glucose is approximately 451 mg/dL?\n\nI. Insulin helps lower blood glucose concentration.\nII. ADH promotes water reabsorption in the kidney.\nIII. Negative feedback helps maintain internal stability.\nIV. Hormones act only on cells that have no receptors for them.","options":["I and II only","I, II and III only","II and IV only","I, II, III and IV"],"answer":1,"explanation":"I, II and III are correct; hormones exert effects through appropriate receptors.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":true},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1060","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"In a large randomly mating population, the frequency of an autosomal recessive allele is 0.18. Assuming Hardy–Weinberg conditions, what is the expected frequency of heterozygotes?","options":["0.30","0.03","0.67","1.00"],"answer":0,"explanation":"With q as the recessive-allele frequency, p=1−q and heterozygotes occur at 2pq.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1061","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"If a producer stores 16,500 kJ of chemical energy and approximately 10% is transferred to the next trophic level, how much energy is available there?","options":["1,650 kJ","165 kJ","8,250 kJ","15,500 kJ"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Using the ecological efficiency approximation, 10% of the energy is transferred to the next trophic level.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1062","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"In a cross between two heterozygous plants with alleles K and k, where K is dominant for large and k is recessive for small, what proportion of offspring is expected to show small?","options":["25%","50%","75%","100%"],"answer":0,"explanation":"A heterozygous × heterozygous cross gives a 1:2:1 genotype ratio and therefore 25% recessive phenotype.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1064","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A plant transpires at an average rate of 6 cm³ of water per hour for 11 hours. How much water is lost in that period?","options":["66 cm³","17 cm³","0.55 cm³","72 cm³"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Total water loss = rate × time.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1065","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"In a healthy adult, alveolar oxygen partial pressure is 113 mmHg while venous blood oxygen partial pressure is 37 mmHg. Which gas will diffuse from the alveolus into the blood?","options":["Oxygen","Carbon dioxide","Nitrogen","Water vapour"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Oxygen moves down its partial-pressure gradient from alveolar air into venous blood.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1067","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which process most directly contributes to genetic variation by maternal and paternal homologues?","options":["independent assortment","binary fission","mitosis","cytokinesis"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Independent assortment contributes to genetic variation in the stated context.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1068","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A population contains 3400 organisms. In one year there are 218 births, 126 deaths, 72 immigrants and 48 emigrants. What is the net increase?","options":["116","92","24","126"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Net population change = births − deaths + immigration − emigration.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1071","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which hormone is most directly associated with the following physiological effect: increase sodium reabsorption in the kidney?","options":["aldosterone","insulin","thyroxine","ADH"],"answer":0,"explanation":"aldosterone has the stated physiological role.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1072","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which structure is best adapted to speed up impulse conduction?","options":["myelin sheath — speed up impulse conduction","cilia — move mucus and trapped particles","nephrons — filter blood and form urine","red blood cells — transport oxygen efficiently"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Myelin sheath is specialised for the stated function.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1073","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which option correctly matches testes with its principal role?","options":["testes — sperm and testosterone","trachea — air passage","red blood cells — oxygen","palisade cells — photosynthesis"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The selected structure is correctly matched with its principal role.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1074","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"In a large randomly mating population, the frequency of an autosomal recessive allele is 0.19. Assuming Hardy–Weinberg conditions, what is the expected frequency of heterozygotes?","options":["0.31","0.04","0.66","1.00"],"answer":0,"explanation":"With q as the recessive-allele frequency, p=1−q and heterozygotes occur at 2pq.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1075","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"If a producer stores 17,000 kJ of chemical energy and approximately 10% is transferred to the next trophic level, how much energy is available there?","options":["1,700 kJ","170 kJ","8,500 kJ","16,000 kJ"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Using the ecological efficiency approximation, 10% of the energy is transferred to the next trophic level.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1076","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"In a cross between two heterozygous plants with alleles L and l, where L is dominant for long and l is recessive for short, what proportion of offspring is expected to show short?","options":["25%","50%","75%","100%"],"answer":0,"explanation":"A heterozygous × heterozygous cross gives a 1:2:1 genotype ratio and therefore 25% recessive phenotype.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1078","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A plant transpires at an average rate of 2 cm³ of water per hour for 12 hours. How much water is lost in that period?","options":["24 cm³","14 cm³","0.17 cm³","26 cm³"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Total water loss = rate × time.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1079","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"In a healthy adult, alveolar oxygen partial pressure is 115 mmHg while venous blood oxygen partial pressure is 38 mmHg. Which gas will diffuse from the alveolus into the blood?","options":["Oxygen","Carbon dioxide","Nitrogen","Water vapour"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Oxygen moves down its partial-pressure gradient from alveolar air into venous blood.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1081","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which process most directly contributes to genetic variation by gamete union?","options":["random fertilisation","binary fission","mitosis","cytokinesis"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Random fertilisation contributes to genetic variation in the stated context.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1082","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A population contains 3500 organisms. In one year there are 225 births, 130 deaths, 75 immigrants and 50 emigrants. What is the net increase?","options":["120","95","25","130"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Net population change = births − deaths + immigration − emigration.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1085","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which hormone is most directly associated with the following physiological effect: support the stress response and metabolism?","options":["cortisol","insulin","thyroxine","ADH"],"answer":0,"explanation":"cortisol has the stated physiological role.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1086","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which structure is best adapted to permit communication between neurones?","options":["synapses — permit communication between neurones","microvilli — increase absorptive surface area","stomata — regulate gaseous exchange and water loss","mitochondria — carry out aerobic respiration"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Synapses is specialised for the stated function.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1087","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which option correctly matches kidneys with its principal role?","options":["kidneys — excretion and osmoregulation","alveoli — gas exchange","white blood cells — immune defence","root hairs — water absorption"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The selected structure is correctly matched with its principal role.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard 