 hours. How much water is lost in that period?","options":["15 cm³","8 cm³","0.60 cm³","18 cm³"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Total water loss = rate × time.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1093","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"In a healthy adult, alveolar oxygen partial pressure is 117 mmHg while venous blood oxygen partial pressure is 39 mmHg. Which gas will diffuse from the alveolus into the blood?","options":["Oxygen","Carbon dioxide","Nitrogen","Water vapour"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Oxygen moves down its partial-pressure gradient from alveolar air into venous blood.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1095","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which process most directly contributes to genetic variation by DNA replication or repair errors?","options":["mutation","binary fission","mitosis","cytokinesis"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Mutation contributes to genetic variation in the stated context.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1096","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"A population contains 3600 organisms. In one year there are 232 births, 134 deaths, 78 immigrants and 52 emigrants. What is the net increase?","options":["124","98","26","134"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Net population change = births − deaths + immigration − emigration.","image":null,"source":"Gifted Brainz UTME Standard Question Bank 2026","needsReview":false,"createdAt":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","subject":"Biology","roman":false},{"id":"qb-biology-gen-1099","type":"mcq","passageId":"","passage":"","q":"Which h